// Install-time hook for SCS-generated creature scripts.
//
// The hook goes immediately before the anchor: the first block of SCS's per-round action
// choice (the first block that checks GlobalTimerNotExpired("castspell","LOCALS"), skipping
// SCS's first-round preparation and the ranged general AI's retarget block). Above the hook go
// guarded copies of the SCS blocks that must keep running while the engine drives the
// creature: bookkeeping runs (Melf's Minute Meteors, Energy and Star Blades), the creature's
// own special abilities, and every block that does more than an ordinary combat round
// (summoning, dialogue, leaving the area, changing allegiance, death handlers and the like).
// The original blocks stay where they are, so a declining or switched-off engine leaves SCS's
// order untouched. Each hook and copy names its own script, so the engine can tell which of a
// creature's scripts asks.
//
// SCS's cloud blocks above the anchor stand aside while the engine weighs danger zones for the
// creature: its escapes (they set SCS's seencloud timer and run from a cloud or walk at the
// enemy), its mages' run from a Cloudkill before they see the enemy (SetInterrupt and a run from
// the marker it heard, on a marker's shout) and its stand-still while it hears a cloud
// (NoAction() alone, on a marker's shout). They get a last condition that holds when BGSE_Zones
// says no (with no enemy in sight it says yes only when the engine leads the creature out of a
// zone that hurts it); first when their triggers end in an OR group that lacks members, which
// the condition would otherwise join. Those below the anchor stay as they are.
//
// SCS's hunt for enemies the creature no longer sees stands aside, above and below the anchor,
// for every creature the engine drives, which searches with its own senses and abilities
// instead: its chase (blocks that use its chase variables for more than bookkeeping that ends
// with Continue(): the walk or teleport to the party member it last saw, the chase's start and
// end), its free detection casts on its detect timer and its walk to the nearest closed door. So
// does every other pursuit of a creature it does not perceive: triggers that say it sees or
// detects no enemy (or not the one it acts on) and a walk, jump, cast or attack at an enemy or
// party member no trigger says it sees (a phase spider's or a mind flayer's teleport to a party
// member, a dragon's walk to one, the walk to the nearest enemy on an ally's shout), unless the
// creature must be on the party's side for it; and its random walk while an unseen attacker
// puzzles it (the whatthe timer). They get a last condition that holds when BGSE_Search says no
// (first in an OR group that lacks members, as above) and are never copied above the hook.
//
// SCS's scripted teleports (Christopher, 2026-10-26: such powers become real abilities): a cast
// without a spellbook check of a spell that moves the caster (bgse_teleports). One at an enemy, a
// party member or the creature last seen, which a trigger says the creature sees or detects, is a
// jump into the fight (SCS's fiends jump to a weak party member): it stands aside like the hunt and
// is never copied above the hook, as the engine jumps with the creature's own teleport. The
// creatures whose hooked scripts teleport by script get an innate teleport of their own unless
// they have one (bgse_grant_teleport, bgse/setup-bgse.tp2).
//
// SCS's free invisibility (F2f; Christopher, 2026-10-26: thieves hide with their own Hide in
// Shadows): a block whose triggers check no spellbook and whose every action is bookkeeping or a
// spellbook-free cast or application at the creature itself, at least one of a spell that makes its
// target invisible (bgse_invisible; bgse_improved those of Improved Invisibility). It gets a last
// condition that holds when BGSE_Hide says no (first in an OR group that lacks members, as above),
// in place and in its copy above the hook: the engine hides the creature its own way, and for every
// other creature SCS's block runs as before. The thieves whose hooked scripts do that get hide skills
// for their level (bgse_raise_skills, bgse/setup-bgse.tp2). SCS's contingencies and sequencers that
// fire an invisibility (they check the CONTINGENCY_TRIGGERED spell state) are its preparation, which
// stays SCS's: no condition.
//
// Every other creature whose hooked scripts make it invisible for free gets real abilities instead
// (F2f-5; Christopher, 2026-10-27: such powers become real innate abilities, as often as SCS gives
// them): each spell such a block casts or applies at the creature becomes an innate ability of its own,
// an invisibility that is no innate ability the game's own Invisibility or Improved Invisibility
// (bgse_block_gifts). It comes back after the block's own timer, or after a round when SCS gives it
// whenever it fits; when SCS counts its uses, the creature gets that many (bgse_frequency). A creature
// keeps an innate invisibility of its own of the same kind, and a thief hides by its skill instead of a
// plain one (bgse_grant_gifts, bgse_create_gifts).
//
// SCS's preparation (bgse_prep_block; Christopher, 2026-10-28: the engine takes over how creatures
// prepare, first just as SCS does): its prebuffs, cast at once while instantprep is still 0, its
// contingencies and sequencers (ContingencyFired), its chain contingencies (ChainContingencyFired) and
// its first-round casts at the creature itself (openers: they set instantprep to 1). Each such block
// above the anchor gets a last condition that holds when BGSE_Prep says no (first in an OR group that
// lacks members, as above): the engine holds back the openers of a creature it drives, as it chooses
// that round itself, and the rest runs as before unless the creature's orders hold it back. Every
// response of a prebuff, contingency or chain block that casts tells the engine what the creature
// prepared (BGSE_Prepped), before its closing Continue() (bgse_notify). Both name the kind, the cast
// spell and the spell taken from the spellbook, as written. An opener the engine holds still ends SCS's
// preparation: right after it a block with its triggers, BGSE_Prep's answer the other way round, sets
// what the opener sets of SCS's state, without its cast, and lets the engine take that round
// (bgse_opener_twin). SCS's own blocks that end its preparation when no opener fires do not cover
// every one of its settings.
//
// SCS's vanishing exits (bgse_exit_block; Christopher, 2026-10-28: nobody leaves for good): a block
// whose triggers check the creature's own hit points below a limit and whose responses do nothing but
// leave: they destroy the creature or cast a spell at it that removes its target from the game
// (bgse_vanish), with only its own bookkeeping, effects, messages, waits and its dropped inventory
// besides (SCS's Erinyes, Melissan's allies, its mind flayers). It gets a last condition that holds when
// BGSE_Stay says no (first in an OR group that lacks members, as above), in place and in its copy above
// the hook: the engine keeps a creature it drives in the fight unless its orders let it leave, and for
// every other creature SCS's block runs as before. A block that does more (a cutscene, a story variable)
// belongs to its encounter and stays as it is.
//
// The game's own vanishing exits (bgse_own_baf; Christopher, 2026-11-03: the Pirate Mage, a Hobgoblin Wizard
// and a Nymph stay in the fight, Terminsel and Lady Yuth keep their story exits): the same kind of exit in a
// script that is not SCS's runs above SCS's hooked script when it sits higher in the creature's stack. One
// whose triggers check nothing but the creature's own hit points and what it sees, and whose responses keep no
// variable and name no creature, gets the same condition, without a family (bgse_own_exit_block): BGSE_Stay
// goes by the script that decides for the creature, the first hooked one below, and answers no wherever there
// is none. Any other trigger may tie the exit to a story, so such an exit stays as it is. Only compiled scripts
// that may hold one are decompiled (bgse_exit_candidate).
//
// SCS's talk on sight (bgse_talk_baf; Christopher, 2026-11-03: a creature that speaks to the party on sight
// prepares when it sees the party, and the talk comes right after): in SCS's talk-on-sight script (its DMWW_
// marker, no castspell round timer, and every block one that starts the talk with a party member the creature sees
// and has not talked to), each block gets a last condition that holds while BGSE_TalkHold says no (first in an OR
// group that lacks members, as above). Scripted encounters whose scripts do more are designed one by one. The engine holds the talk for a moment and turns on SCS's own switch for preparing
// out of sight, so the creature's prebuffs run first, with SCS's difficulty rules (combat-intent/talk.lua).
//
// tools/hook_rule.py is the reference version of this rule. Keep the two in step;
// tests/integration/test_hook_installer.py compares them.

// The lines of bgse_text that bgse_regexp matches, a regexp that matches within one line from its
// start to its end, each with its line end, in their order. REPLACE_EVALUATE copies its whole text
// for each match, so a pass over a whole script goes over these lines instead.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_matching_lines
  STR_VAR bgse_text = ~~
          bgse_regexp = ~~
  RET bgse_lines
BEGIN
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_lines ~~
  INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_text%~ BEGIN
    SET p = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~%bgse_regexp%~)
    WHILE (p >= 0) BEGIN
      SET e = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%~ p)
      PATCH_IF (e < 0) BEGIN
        SET e = BUFFER_LENGTH
      END
      READ_ASCII p line (e - p)
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_lines ~%bgse_lines%%line%%LNL%~
      SET p = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~%bgse_regexp%~ e)
    END
  END
END

// The spells of a script's casts without a spellbook (ForceSpell, ReallyForceSpell and their Point
// and RES forms) as |R=RESREF| and |I=NAME| entries in upper case, each once: the RES forms name
// the resource first, the others name the spell (a SPELL.IDS name or number) last. bgse_text is the
// script without its comments (bgse_hook_bcs).
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_cast_spells
  STR_VAR bgse_text = ~~
  RET bgse_spells
BEGIN
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_spells ~|~
  TEXT_SPRINT casts ~^    \(ReallyForceSpellPointRES\|ReallyForceSpellPoint\|ReallyForceSpellRES\|ReallyForceSpell\|ForceSpellPointRES\|ForceSpellPoint\|ForceSpellRES\|ForceSpell\)(\(.*\)) *$~
  LPF bgse_matching_lines STR_VAR bgse_text = EVAL ~%bgse_text%~ bgse_regexp = EVAL ~%casts%~ RET bgse_lines END
  INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_lines%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~%casts%~ BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT action ~%MATCH1%~
      TEXT_SPRINT args ~%MATCH2%~
      LPF bgse_cast_parts STR_VAR bgse_action = EVAL ~%action%~ bgse_args = EVAL ~%args%~ RET bgse_spell bgse_target END
      TEXT_SPRINT form ~I~
      PATCH_IF ((~%action%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^.*RES$~) = 0) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT form ~R~
      END
      PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_spell%~ > 0)
          AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%form%=%bgse_spell%|~ ~%bgse_spells%~) < 0) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT bgse_spells ~%bgse_spells%%form%=%bgse_spell%|~
      END
    END ~%MATCH0%~
  END
END

// The spell (in upper case unless bgse_upper is 0, without quotes) and the target of one such cast,
// its action and the text between its brackets (tools/hook_rule.py: ungated_casts, spell_and_target);
// the target is empty for a cast at a point.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_cast_parts
  INT_VAR bgse_upper = 1
  STR_VAR bgse_action = ~~
          bgse_args = ~~
  RET bgse_spell bgse_target
BEGIN
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_spell ~~
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_target ~~
  PATCH_IF ((~%bgse_action%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^.*RES$~) = 0) BEGIN
    SET comma = INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~,~ ~%bgse_args%~)
  END ELSE BEGIN
    SET comma = RINDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~,~ ~%bgse_args%~)
  END
  INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_args%~ BEGIN
    PATCH_IF (comma < 0) BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0 bgse_spell (BUFFER_LENGTH)
    END ELSE PATCH_IF ((~%bgse_action%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^.*RES$~) = 0) BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0 bgse_spell (comma)
      READ_ASCII (comma + 1) bgse_target (BUFFER_LENGTH - comma - 1)
    END ELSE BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0 bgse_target (comma)
      READ_ASCII (comma + 1) bgse_spell (BUFFER_LENGTH - comma - 1)
    END
  END
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE bgse_spell ~%bgse_spell%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~"~ ~~
  END
  PATCH_IF (bgse_upper = 1) BEGIN
    TO_UPPER bgse_spell
  END
  PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~Point~ ~%bgse_action%~) >= 0) BEGIN
    TEXT_SPRINT bgse_target ~~
  END
END

// The resref of a spell as a script names it: bgse_form R names a resref, I a SPELL.IDS name or
// number; empty when the game's SPELL.IDS lacks the name or the number is no spell's.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_spell_res
  STR_VAR bgse_form = ~R~
          bgse_spell = ~~
  RET bgse_res
BEGIN
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_res ~%bgse_spell%~
  PATCH_IF (~%bgse_form%~ STRING_EQUAL ~I~) BEGIN
    PATCH_IF ((~%bgse_spell%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^[0-9]+$~) = 0) BEGIN
      SET number = bgse_spell
    END ELSE BEGIN
      SET number = IDS_OF_SYMBOL (~SPELL~ ~%bgse_spell%~)
    END
    TEXT_SPRINT bgse_res ~~
    PATCH_IF (number >= 1000) AND (number < 5000) BEGIN
      SET kind = number / 1000
      SET rest = number - kind * 1000
      TEXT_SPRINT prefix ~SPCL~
      PATCH_IF (kind = 1) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT prefix ~SPPR~
      END ELSE PATCH_IF (kind = 2) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT prefix ~SPWI~
      END ELSE PATCH_IF (kind = 3) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT prefix ~SPIN~
      END
      PATCH_IF (rest < 10) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT bgse_res ~%prefix%00%rest%~
      END ELSE PATCH_IF (rest < 100) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT bgse_res ~%prefix%0%rest%~
      END ELSE BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT bgse_res ~%prefix%%rest%~
      END
    END
  END
END

// Whether a spell moves its caster: an ability with opcode 124 (Teleport) or 274 (Teleport to
// target) on the caster (target 1). bgse_form as in bgse_spell_res. A spell the game lacks moves
// nobody.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_moves_caster
  STR_VAR bgse_form = ~R~
          bgse_spell = ~~
  RET bgse_moves
BEGIN
  SET bgse_moves = 0
  LPF bgse_spell_res STR_VAR bgse_form = EVAL ~%bgse_form%~ bgse_spell = EVAL ~%bgse_spell%~ RET bgse_res END
  TEXT_SPRINT res ~%bgse_res%~
  PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%res%~ > 0) AND (STRING_LENGTH ~%res%~ <= 8) BEGIN
    PATCH_IF (FILE_EXISTS_IN_GAME ~%res%.spl~) BEGIN
      INNER_PATCH_FILE ~%res%.spl~ BEGIN
        PATCH_IF (BUFFER_LENGTH >= 0x72) BEGIN
          READ_ASCII 0 signature (8)
          PATCH_IF (~%signature%~ STRING_EQUAL ~SPL V1  ~) BEGIN
            READ_LONG 0x64 abilities
            READ_SHORT 0x68 ability_count
            READ_LONG 0x6a effects
            FOR (a = 0; a < ability_count; a += 1) BEGIN
              SET at = abilities + 0x28 * a
              PATCH_IF (at + 0x28 <= BUFFER_LENGTH) BEGIN
                READ_SHORT (at + 0x1e) effect_count
                READ_SHORT (at + 0x20) first
                FOR (f = 0; f < effect_count; f += 1) BEGIN
                  SET e = effects + 0x30 * (first + f)
                  PATCH_IF (e + 0x30 <= BUFFER_LENGTH) BEGIN
                    READ_SHORT e opcode
                    READ_BYTE (e + 2) target
                    PATCH_IF ((opcode = 124) OR (opcode = 274)) AND (target = 1) BEGIN
                      SET bgse_moves = 1
                    END
                  END
                END
              END
            END
          END
        END
      END
    END
  END
END

// Whether a spell makes its target invisible: 1 when an ability has opcode 20 (Invisibility) on
// the caster or on the spell's target (target 1 or 2), 2 when one such is Improved Invisibility
// (parameter 2 is 1); 0 for a spell the game lacks. bgse_innate_spell is 1 when its file says it is
// an innate ability (type 4), bgse_removing when an ability has opcode 68 (Unsummon creature: it
// removes the creature from the game) on the caster or on the spell's target. bgse_form as in
// bgse_spell_res.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_hides_target
  STR_VAR bgse_form = ~R~
          bgse_spell = ~~
  RET bgse_hiding bgse_innate_spell bgse_removing
BEGIN
  SET bgse_hiding = 0
  SET bgse_innate_spell = 0
  SET bgse_removing = 0
  LPF bgse_spell_res STR_VAR bgse_form = EVAL ~%bgse_form%~ bgse_spell = EVAL ~%bgse_spell%~ RET bgse_res END
  TEXT_SPRINT res ~%bgse_res%~
  PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%res%~ > 0) AND (STRING_LENGTH ~%res%~ <= 8) BEGIN
    PATCH_IF (FILE_EXISTS_IN_GAME ~%res%.spl~) BEGIN
      INNER_PATCH_FILE ~%res%.spl~ BEGIN
        PATCH_IF (BUFFER_LENGTH >= 0x72) BEGIN
          READ_ASCII 0 signature (8)
          PATCH_IF (~%signature%~ STRING_EQUAL ~SPL V1  ~) BEGIN
            READ_SHORT 0x1c spell_type
            SET bgse_innate_spell = (spell_type = 4) ? 1 : 0
            READ_LONG 0x64 abilities
            READ_SHORT 0x68 ability_count
            READ_LONG 0x6a effects
            FOR (a = 0; a < ability_count; a += 1) BEGIN
              SET at = abilities + 0x28 * a
              PATCH_IF (at + 0x28 <= BUFFER_LENGTH) BEGIN
                READ_SHORT (at + 0x1e) effect_count
                READ_SHORT (at + 0x20) first
                FOR (f = 0; f < effect_count; f += 1) BEGIN
                  SET e = effects + 0x30 * (first + f)
                  PATCH_IF (e + 0x30 <= BUFFER_LENGTH) BEGIN
                    READ_SHORT e opcode
                    READ_BYTE (e + 2) target
                    READ_LONG (e + 8) kind
                    PATCH_IF (opcode = 20) AND ((target = 1) OR (target = 2)) BEGIN
                      PATCH_IF (kind = 1) BEGIN
                        SET bgse_hiding = 2
                      END ELSE PATCH_IF (bgse_hiding = 0) BEGIN
                        SET bgse_hiding = 1
                      END
                    END
                    PATCH_IF (opcode = 68) AND ((target = 1) OR (target = 2)) BEGIN
                      SET bgse_removing = 1
                    END
                  END
                END
              END
            END
          END
        END
      END
    END
  END
END

// Look a spell up in the game once (bgse_hides_target): bgse_looked lists the spells looked up so
// far, bgse_invisible those that make their target invisible, bgse_improved those of Improved
// Invisibility, bgse_innate those whose files say innate and bgse_vanish those that remove their
// target from the game (|NAME| entries in upper case, as scripts name them; bgse_form as in
// bgse_spell_res).
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_look_spell
  STR_VAR bgse_form = ~R~
          bgse_spell = ~~
          bgse_looked = ~|~
          bgse_invisible = ~|~
          bgse_improved = ~|~
          bgse_innate = ~|~
          bgse_vanish = ~|~
  RET bgse_looked bgse_invisible bgse_improved bgse_innate bgse_vanish
BEGIN
  PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%bgse_spell%|~ ~%bgse_looked%~) < 0) BEGIN
    LPF bgse_hides_target STR_VAR bgse_form = EVAL ~%bgse_form%~ bgse_spell = EVAL ~%bgse_spell%~
      RET bgse_hiding bgse_innate_spell bgse_removing END
    TEXT_SPRINT bgse_looked ~%bgse_looked%%bgse_spell%|~
    PATCH_IF (bgse_hiding > 0) BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_invisible ~%bgse_invisible%%bgse_spell%|~
    END
    PATCH_IF (bgse_hiding = 2) BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_improved ~%bgse_improved%%bgse_spell%|~
    END
    PATCH_IF (bgse_innate_spell = 1) BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_innate ~%bgse_innate%%bgse_spell%|~
    END
    PATCH_IF (bgse_removing = 1) BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_vanish ~%bgse_vanish%%bgse_spell%|~
    END
  END
END

// The spells of a script's casts and applications at the creature itself without a spellbook
// (ApplySpell, ForceSpell, ReallyForceSpell, SpellNoDec and their RES forms, at Myself) as |R=RESREF|
// and |I=NAME| entries in upper case, each once (tools/hook_rule.py: self_spells). bgse_text is the
// script without its comments (bgse_hook_bcs).
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_self_spells
  STR_VAR bgse_text = ~~
  RET bgse_spells
BEGIN
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_spells ~|~
  TEXT_SPRINT by_res ~^    \(ApplySpellRES\|ForceSpellRES\|ReallyForceSpellRES\|SpellNoDecRES\)("\([^"]*\)",Myself) *$~
  LPF bgse_matching_lines STR_VAR bgse_text = EVAL ~%bgse_text%~ bgse_regexp = EVAL ~%by_res%~ RET bgse_lines END
  INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_lines%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~%by_res%~ BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH2%~
      TO_UPPER name
      PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%name%~ > 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|R=%name%|~ ~%bgse_spells%~) < 0) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT bgse_spells ~%bgse_spells%R=%name%|~
      END
    END ~%MATCH0%~
  END
  TEXT_SPRINT by_name ~^    \(ApplySpell\|ForceSpell\|ReallyForceSpell\|SpellNoDec\)(Myself,\([^,()" ]+\)) *$~
  LPF bgse_matching_lines STR_VAR bgse_text = EVAL ~%bgse_text%~ bgse_regexp = EVAL ~%by_name%~ RET bgse_lines END
  INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_lines%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~%by_name%~ BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH2%~
      TO_UPPER name
      PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|I=%name%|~ ~%bgse_spells%~) < 0) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT bgse_spells ~%bgse_spells%I=%name%|~
      END
    END ~%MATCH0%~
  END
END

// The free invisibility a block gives the creature (tools/hook_rule.py: free_hide): 0 for none, 1
// plain, 2 improved. Its triggers check no spellbook, every action is bookkeeping (SetGlobal,
// SetGlobalTimer, SetGlobalTimerRandom, IncrementGlobal, Continue, DisplayString, DisplayStringHead)
// or a cast or application at the creature itself without a spellbook, and at least one of those
// casts a spell that makes its target invisible (bgse_invisible; bgse_improved those of Improved
// Invisibility, |NAME| entries in upper case). Not SCS's contingencies and sequencers, which check the
// CONTINGENCY_TRIGGERED spell state: they are its preparation. Comments go first.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_hide_block
  STR_VAR bgse_block = ~~
          bgse_invisible = ~|~
          bgse_improved = ~|~
  RET bgse_hide
BEGIN
  SET bgse_hide = 0
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE text ~%bgse_block%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~ *//.*$~ ~~
  END
  TEXT_SPRINT trig ~~
  TEXT_SPRINT resp ~~
  INNER_PATCH ~%text%~ BEGIN
    SET then = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~)
    PATCH_IF (then > 0) BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0 trig (then)
      READ_ASCII then resp (BUFFER_LENGTH - then)
    END
  END
  // Only a block with a cast or application at the creature itself can give it (in any case, as
  // below), so the others need no look at each action.
  PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%resp%~ > 0)
      AND ((~%trig%~ STRING_CONTAINS_REGEXP ~[^A-Za-z0-9_]\(HaveSpell\|HaveSpellRES\|HasItem\|KnowSpell\)(~) != 0)
      AND ((~%trig%~ STRING_CONTAINS_REGEXP ~^ +!?CheckSpellState(Myself,CONTINGENCY_TRIGGERED) *$~) != 0)
      AND (INDEX (CASE_INSENSITIVE ~^    \(\(ApplySpellRES\|ForceSpellRES\|ReallyForceSpellRES\|SpellNoDecRES\)("[^"]*",Myself)\|\(ApplySpell\|ForceSpell\|ReallyForceSpell\|SpellNoDec\)(Myself,[^,()" ]+)\) *$~ ~%resp%~) >= 0) BEGIN
    SET kind = 0
    SET foreign = 0
    INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    \([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\)(.*$~ BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT action ~%MATCH1%~
        TEXT_SPRINT line ~%MATCH0%~
        PATCH_IF ((~%action%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^\(SetGlobal\|SetGlobalTimer\|SetGlobalTimerRandom\|IncrementGlobal\|Continue\|DisplayString\|DisplayStringHead\)$~) != 0) BEGIN
          SET self = 0
          TEXT_SPRINT name ~~
          PATCH_IF ((~%line%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^    \(ApplySpellRES\|ForceSpellRES\|ReallyForceSpellRES\|SpellNoDecRES\)("[^"]*",Myself) *$~) = 0) BEGIN
            SET self = 1
            INNER_PATCH ~%line%~ BEGIN
              REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~"\([^"]*\)"~ BEGIN
                TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH1%~
              END ~%MATCH0%~
            END
          END ELSE PATCH_IF ((~%line%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^    \(ApplySpell\|ForceSpell\|ReallyForceSpell\|SpellNoDec\)(Myself,[^,()" ]+) *$~) = 0) BEGIN
            SET self = 1
            INNER_PATCH ~%line%~ BEGIN
              REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~(Myself,\([^,()" ]+\))~ BEGIN
                TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH1%~
              END ~%MATCH0%~
            END
          END
          PATCH_IF (self = 0) BEGIN
            SET foreign += 1
          END ELSE PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%name%~ > 0) BEGIN
            TO_UPPER name
            PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%|~ ~%bgse_improved%~) >= 0) BEGIN
              SET kind = 2
            END ELSE PATCH_IF (kind = 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%|~ ~%bgse_invisible%~) >= 0) BEGIN
              SET kind = 1
            END
          END
        END
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
    SET bgse_hide = (foreign = 0) ? kind : 0
  END
END

// Whether a block is one of SCS's vanishing exits (tools/hook_rule.py: is_exit): its triggers check the
// creature's own hit points below a limit above 0 (HPPercentLT or HPLT at Myself, two spaces in: not
// negated, not one of an OR group), and its responses do nothing but leave. At least one action destroys
// the creature (DestroySelf()) or casts or applies at it without a spellbook a spell that removes its
// target (bgse_vanish, |NAME| entries in upper case, the forms bgse_self_spells reads); every other one is
// SetGlobal, SetGlobalTimer, SetGlobalTimerRandom or IncrementGlobal on the creature's own LOCALS
// variables, Continue, DisplayString, DisplayStringHead, CreateVisualEffect, CreateVisualEffectObject,
// PlaySound, SmallWait, Wait or DropInventory. Comments go first.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_exit_block
  STR_VAR bgse_block = ~~
          bgse_vanish = ~|~
  RET bgse_exit
BEGIN
  SET bgse_exit = 0
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE text ~%bgse_block%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~ *//.*$~ ~~
  END
  TEXT_SPRINT trig ~~
  TEXT_SPRINT resp ~~
  INNER_PATCH ~%text%~ BEGIN
    SET then = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~)
    PATCH_IF (then > 0) BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0 trig (then)
      READ_ASCII then resp (BUFFER_LENGTH - then)
    END
  END
  PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%resp%~ > 0)
      AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^  \(HPPercentLT\|HPLT\)(Myself,[1-9][0-9]*) *$~ ~%trig%~) >= 0) BEGIN
    SET leaves = 0
    SET other = 0
    INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    \([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\)(.*$~ BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT action ~%MATCH1%~
        TEXT_SPRINT line ~%MATCH0%~
        TEXT_SPRINT name ~~
        PATCH_IF ((~%line%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^    \(ApplySpellRES\|ForceSpellRES\|ReallyForceSpellRES\|SpellNoDecRES\)("[^"]*",Myself) *$~) = 0) BEGIN
          INNER_PATCH ~%line%~ BEGIN
            REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~"\([^"]*\)"~ BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH1%~
            END ~%MATCH0%~
          END
        END ELSE PATCH_IF ((~%line%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^    \(ApplySpell\|ForceSpell\|ReallyForceSpell\|SpellNoDec\)(Myself,[^,()" ]+) *$~) = 0) BEGIN
          INNER_PATCH ~%line%~ BEGIN
            REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~(Myself,\([^,()" ]+\))~ BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH1%~
            END ~%MATCH0%~
          END
        END
        TO_UPPER name
        PATCH_IF ((~%line%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^    DestroySelf() *$~) = 0)
            OR ((STRING_LENGTH ~%name%~ > 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%|~ ~%bgse_vanish%~) >= 0)) BEGIN
          SET leaves += 1
        END ELSE PATCH_IF ((~%action%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^\(SetGlobal\|SetGlobalTimer\|SetGlobalTimerRandom\|IncrementGlobal\|Continue\|DisplayString\|DisplayStringHead\|CreateVisualEffect\|CreateVisualEffectObject\|PlaySound\|SmallWait\|Wait\|DropInventory\)$~) != 0) BEGIN
          SET other += 1
        END ELSE PATCH_IF ((~%action%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^\(SetGlobal\|SetGlobalTimer\|SetGlobalTimerRandom\|IncrementGlobal\)$~) = 0)
            AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    [A-Za-z]+("[^"]*","LOCALS",~ ~%line%~) != 0) BEGIN
          SET other += 1
        END
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
    SET bgse_exit = ((leaves > 0) AND (other = 0)) ? 1 : 0
  END
END

// Whether a block is one of the game's own vanishing exits that no story decides (tools/hook_rule.py:
// is_own_exit): a vanishing exit (bgse_exit_block) whose every trigger checks the creature's own hit points (HP,
// HPGT, HPLT, HPPercent, HPPercentGT or HPPercentLT at Myself) or what it sees (See or Detect, negated or not,
// with nothing quoted: no named creature), two spaces in (no OR group), and whose responses quote nothing but
// a resource (the first argument of ApplySpellRES, ForceSpellRES, ReallyForceSpellRES, SpellNoDecRES,
// CreateVisualEffect, CreateVisualEffectObject or PlaySound), so they set no variable and name no creature.
// Comments go first.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_own_exit_block
  STR_VAR bgse_block = ~~
          bgse_vanish = ~|~
  RET bgse_exit
BEGIN
  LPF bgse_exit_block STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%bgse_block%~ bgse_vanish = EVAL ~%bgse_vanish%~ RET bgse_exit END
  PATCH_IF (bgse_exit = 1) BEGIN
    INNER_PATCH_SAVE text ~%bgse_block%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~ *//.*$~ ~~
    END
    SET then = INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~ ~%text%~)
    INNER_PATCH ~%text%~ BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0 trig (then)
      READ_ASCII then resp (BUFFER_LENGTH - then)
    END
    SET other = 0
    INNER_PATCH ~%trig%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^.+$~ BEGIN
        PATCH_IF ((~%MATCH0%~ STRING_EQUAL ~IF~) = 0)
            AND ((~%MATCH0%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^  !?\(HP\|HPGT\|HPLT\|HPPercent\|HPPercentGT\|HPPercentLT\)(Myself,[0-9]+) *$~) != 0)
            AND ((~%MATCH0%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^  !?\(See\|Detect\)([^"]*) *$~) != 0) BEGIN
          SET other += 1
        END
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
    INNER_PATCH_SAVE named ~%resp%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~^\(    \(ApplySpellRES\|ForceSpellRES\|ReallyForceSpellRES\|SpellNoDecRES\|CreateVisualEffect\|CreateVisualEffectObject\|PlaySound\)(\)"[^"]*"~ ~\1~
    END
    PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~"~ ~%named%~) >= 0) BEGIN
      SET other += 1
    END
    SET bgse_exit = (other = 0) ? 1 : 0
  END
END

// The game's own vanishing exits in one decompiled script (tools/hook_rule.py: patch_own; Christopher,
// 2026-11-03: the Pirate Mage, a Hobgoblin Wizard and a Nymph stay in the fight, Terminsel and Lady Yuth keep
// their story exits). bgse_script is its resref in lower case and bgse_vanish the spells that remove their
// target (as in bgse_exit_block). Each exit that no story decides (bgse_own_exit_block) gets a last condition
// that holds when BGSE_Stay says no, with no family: BGSE_Stay goes by the script that decides for the creature
// (kernel/hook.lua, driver). bgse_exits counts them. A script of SCS's (DMWW_ in it), one patched before
// (BGSE_Stay in it) and one whose name cannot go into Lua text stay as they are. bgse_baf comes back without
// carriage returns, as bgse_hook_baf gives it.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_own_baf
  STR_VAR bgse_baf = ~~
          bgse_script = ~~
          bgse_vanish = ~|~
  RET bgse_exits bgse_baf
BEGIN
  SET bgse_exits = 0
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE bgse_baf ~%bgse_baf%~ BEGIN
    PATCH_IF (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%MNL%~) >= 0) BEGIN
      REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%MNL%~ ~~
    END
    PATCH_IF (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~DMWW_~) < 0) AND (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~BGSE_Stay~) < 0)
        AND (INDEX (EXACT_MATCH ~'~ ~%bgse_script%~) < 0) AND (INDEX (EXACT_MATCH ~"~ ~%bgse_script%~) < 0)
        AND (INDEX (EXACT_MATCH ~\~ ~%bgse_script%~) < 0) BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT stay_line ~  !EEex_LuaTrigger("return BGSE_Stay and BGSE_Stay(EEex_LuaTrigger_Object,'','%bgse_script%') or false")~
      SET pos = 0
      WHILE (pos >= 0) BEGIN
        SET stop = 0 - 1
        SET start = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^IF%LNL%~ pos)
        PATCH_IF (start >= 0) BEGIN
          SET end = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%END%LNL%~ start)
          PATCH_IF (end >= 0) BEGIN
            SET stop = end + 5
          END
        END
        PATCH_IF (stop < 0) BEGIN
          SET pos = 0 - 1
        END ELSE BEGIN
          SET pos = stop
          READ_ASCII start block (stop - start)
          PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^  \(HPPercentLT\|HPLT\)(Myself,~ ~%block%~) >= 0) BEGIN
            LPF bgse_own_exit_block STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%block%~ bgse_vanish = EVAL ~%bgse_vanish%~ RET bgse_exit END
            PATCH_IF (bgse_exit = 1) BEGIN
              LPF bgse_aside INT_VAR bgse_from = start bgse_to = stop STR_VAR bgse_lines = EVAL ~%stay_line%~ END
              SET pos = stop + STRING_LENGTH ~%LNL%%stay_line%~
              SET bgse_exits += 1
            END
          END
        END
      END
    END
  END
END

// Whether the compiled script in the patch buffer may hold a vanishing exit, so that only such scripts are
// decompiled (bgse_own_bcs): a block with a hit point trigger (bgse_hurt, its compiled form: TR and the
// trigger's number from TRIGGER.IDS) and an action that destroys the creature or casts or applies a spell
// (bgse_leave: AC and the action's number from ACTION.IDS). A block runs from its CR and CO to the next.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_exit_candidate
  STR_VAR bgse_hurt = ~~
          bgse_leave = ~~
  RET bgse_candidate
BEGIN
  SET bgse_candidate = 0
  SET p = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~%bgse_hurt%~)
  WHILE (p >= 0) BEGIN
    SET next = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~CR%LNL%CO%LNL%~ p)
    PATCH_IF (next < 0) BEGIN
      SET next = BUFFER_LENGTH
    END
    SET a = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~%bgse_leave%~ p)
    PATCH_IF (a >= 0) AND (a < next) BEGIN
      SET bgse_candidate = 1
      SET p = 0 - 1
    END ELSE PATCH_IF (next < BUFFER_LENGTH) BEGIN
      SET p = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~%bgse_hurt%~ next)
    END ELSE BEGIN
      SET p = 0 - 1
    END
  END
END

// The compiled forms bgse_exit_candidate looks for, from the game's TRIGGER.IDS and ACTION.IDS: bgse_hurt a
// trigger HPLT or HPPercentLT at a limit above 0, bgse_leave an action DestroySelf, ApplySpell, ForceSpell,
// ReallyForceSpell, SpellNoDec or one of their RES forms (which share their numbers in the game's ACTION.IDS).
// Each is empty when the game has none of them.
DEFINE_ACTION_FUNCTION bgse_exit_patterns
  RET bgse_hurt bgse_leave
BEGIN
  OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT hurt ~~
  ACTION_FOR_EACH name IN ~HPLT~ ~HPPercentLT~ BEGIN
    OUTER_SET id = IDS_OF_SYMBOL (~TRIGGER~ ~%name%~)
    ACTION_IF (id >= 0) BEGIN
      ACTION_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%hurt%~ > 0) BEGIN
        OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT hurt ~%hurt%\|~
      END
      OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT hurt ~%hurt%%id%~
    END
  END
  OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT leave ~~
  ACTION_FOR_EACH name IN ~DestroySelf~ ~ApplySpell~ ~ApplySpellRES~ ~ForceSpell~ ~ForceSpellRES~ ~ReallyForceSpell~
      ~ReallyForceSpellRES~ ~SpellNoDec~ ~SpellNoDecRES~ BEGIN
    OUTER_SET id = IDS_OF_SYMBOL (~ACTION~ ~%name%~)
    ACTION_IF (id >= 0) BEGIN
      ACTION_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%leave%~ > 0) BEGIN
        OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT leave ~%leave%\|~
      END
      OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT leave ~%leave%%id%~
    END
  END
  OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT bgse_hurt ~~
  OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT bgse_leave ~~
  ACTION_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%hurt%~ > 0) AND (STRING_LENGTH ~%leave%~ > 0) BEGIN
    OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT bgse_hurt ~TR%LNL%\(%hurt%\) [1-9][0-9]* ~
    OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT bgse_leave ~AC%LNL%\(%leave%\)OB~
  END
END

// The compiled form of a fight action, for the engine's own hook (setup-bgse.tp2; tools/hook_rule.py: fights):
// AC and the number the game's ACTION.IDS gives an attack or a cast (the RES forms share their numbers).
// Empty when the game has none of them.
DEFINE_ACTION_FUNCTION bgse_fight_pattern
  RET bgse_fight
BEGIN
  OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT fight ~~
  ACTION_FOR_EACH name IN ~Attack~ ~AttackNoSound~ ~AttackOneRound~ ~AttackReevaluate~ ~Spell~ ~SpellRES~ ~SpellPoint~
      ~SpellPointRES~ ~ForceSpell~ ~ForceSpellRES~ ~ForceSpellPoint~ ~ForceSpellPointRES~ ~ReallyForceSpell~
      ~ReallyForceSpellRES~ ~ReallyForceSpellPoint~ ~ReallyForceSpellPointRES~ ~SpellNoDec~ ~SpellNoDecRES~
      ~SpellPointNoDec~ ~SpellPointNoDecRES~ BEGIN
    OUTER_SET id = IDS_OF_SYMBOL (~ACTION~ ~%name%~)
    ACTION_IF (id >= 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%id%|~ ~|%fight%|~) < 0) BEGIN
      ACTION_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%fight%~ > 0) BEGIN
        OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT fight ~%fight%|~
      END
      OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT fight ~%fight%%id%~
    END
  END
  OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT bgse_fight ~~
  ACTION_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%fight%~ > 0) BEGIN
    OUTER_INNER_PATCH_SAVE fight ~%fight%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|~ ~\|~
    END
    OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT bgse_fight ~AC%LNL%\(%fight%\)OB~
  END
END

// The game's own vanishing exits in the BCS in the patch buffer (bgse_own_baf); bgse_script is its resref in
// lower case. The spells of its casts and applications at the creature itself are looked up in the game once
// each (bgse_look_spell), and the lists come back with them. A script that fails to decompile, patch or compile
// is left exactly as it was (bgse_exits 0).
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_own_bcs
  STR_VAR bgse_script = ~~
          bgse_invisible = ~|~
          bgse_improved = ~|~
          bgse_innate = ~|~
          bgse_vanish = ~|~
          bgse_looked = ~|~
  RET bgse_exits bgse_invisible bgse_improved bgse_innate bgse_vanish bgse_looked
BEGIN
  SET bgse_exits = 0
  READ_ASCII 0 bcs (BUFFER_LENGTH)
  PATCH_TRY
    INNER_PATCH_SAVE baf ~%bcs%~ BEGIN
      DECOMPILE_BCS_TO_BAF
    END
    INNER_PATCH_SAVE text ~%baf%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~ *//.*$~ ~~
    END
    LPF bgse_self_spells STR_VAR bgse_text = EVAL ~%text%~ RET bgse_spells END
    INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_spells%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~\([RI]\)=\([^|]+\)~ BEGIN
        LPF bgse_look_spell STR_VAR bgse_form = EVAL ~%MATCH1%~ bgse_spell = EVAL ~%MATCH2%~ bgse_looked = EVAL ~%bgse_looked%~
            bgse_invisible = EVAL ~%bgse_invisible%~ bgse_improved = EVAL ~%bgse_improved%~ bgse_innate = EVAL ~%bgse_innate%~
            bgse_vanish = EVAL ~%bgse_vanish%~
          RET bgse_looked bgse_invisible bgse_improved bgse_innate bgse_vanish END
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
    LPF bgse_own_baf STR_VAR bgse_baf = EVAL ~%baf%~ bgse_script = EVAL ~%bgse_script%~ bgse_vanish = EVAL ~%bgse_vanish%~
      RET bgse_exits bgse_baf END
    PATCH_IF (bgse_exits > 0) BEGIN
      DELETE_BYTES 0 BUFFER_LENGTH
      INSERT_BYTES 0 (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_baf%~)
      WRITE_ASCIIE 0 ~%bgse_baf%~
      COMPILE_BAF_TO_BCS
    END
  WITH DEFAULT
    SET bgse_exits = 0
    DELETE_BYTES 0 BUFFER_LENGTH
    INSERT_BYTES 0 (STRING_LENGTH ~%bcs%~)
    WRITE_ASCIIE 0 ~%bcs%~
  END
END

// Whether a block of a decompiled script is SCS's talk on sight (tools/hook_rule.py: is_talk):
// NumTimesTalkedTo(0) and See([PC]) among its triggers, and a response that starts the talk with that party
// member (Dialog or StartDialogNoSet at [PC]). Comments do not count.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_talk_block
  INT_VAR bgse_own = 0
  STR_VAR bgse_block = ~~
  RET bgse_talk
BEGIN
  SET bgse_talk = 0
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE text ~%bgse_block%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~ *//.*$~ ~~
  END
  SET then = INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~ ~%text%~)
  PATCH_IF (then >= 0) BEGIN
    INNER_PATCH ~%text%~ BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0 trig (then)
      READ_ASCII then resp (BUFFER_LENGTH - then)
    END
    SET starts_talk = 0
    PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    \(Dialog\|Dialogue\|StartDialogNoSet\|StartDialogueNoSet\)(\[PC\]) *$~ ~%resp%~) >= 0) BEGIN
      SET starts_talk = 1
    END ELSE PATCH_IF (bgse_own = 1)
        AND ((INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    \(Dialog\|Dialogue\|StartDialogNoSet\|StartDialogueNoSet\|StartDialogNoSetInterrupt\|StartDialogueNoSetInterrupt\)(\(\[PC\]\|LastSeenBy\|LastSeenBy(Myself)\)) *$~ ~%resp%~) >= 0)
             OR (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    \(StartDialog\|StartDialogue\)("[^"]+",\(\[PC\]\|LastSeenBy\|LastSeenBy(Myself)\)) *$~ ~%resp%~) >= 0)) BEGIN
      SET starts_talk = 1
    END
    PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^ +NumTimesTalkedTo(0) *$~ ~%trig%~) >= 0)
        AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^ +See(\[PC\]) *$~ ~%trig%~) >= 0)
        AND (starts_talk = 1) BEGIN
      SET bgse_talk = 1
    END
  END
END

// SCS's talk on sight in one decompiled script (tools/hook_rule.py: patch_talk; Christopher, 2026-11-03: a
// creature that speaks to the party on sight prepares when it sees the party, and the talk comes right after).
// bgse_script is its resref in lower case. In a script with SCS's DMWW_ marker, no castspell round timer and every
// block a talk on sight (bgse_talk_block: SCS gives such a script to the creatures that talk to the party on sight
// and then fight), each block gets a condition that holds while BGSE_TalkHold says no, with no family: last, first
// when its triggers end in an OR group that lacks members (bgse_aside). bgse_talks counts them. A scripted
// encounter whose script does more (SCS's Icharyd and his storm), a script patched before (BGSE_TalkHold in it)
// and one whose name cannot go into Lua text stay as they are. bgse_own 1: a designed creature's own copy of a talk
// script (bgse/lib/encounter.tpa, such as Karlat's copy of the game's INITDLG): no SCS marker needed, and only its
// talk blocks get the condition. bgse_baf comes back without carriage returns, as bgse_hook_baf gives it.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_talk_baf
  INT_VAR bgse_own = 0
  STR_VAR bgse_baf = ~~
          bgse_script = ~~
  RET bgse_talks bgse_baf
BEGIN
  SET bgse_talks = 0
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE bgse_baf ~%bgse_baf%~ BEGIN
    PATCH_IF (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%MNL%~) >= 0) BEGIN
      REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%MNL%~ ~~
    END
    SET scs = ((INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~DMWW_~) >= 0) AND (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~castspell~) < 0)) ? 1 : 0
    PATCH_IF ((scs = 1) OR (bgse_own = 1))
        AND (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~BGSE_TalkHold~) < 0)
        AND (INDEX (EXACT_MATCH ~'~ ~%bgse_script%~) < 0) AND (INDEX (EXACT_MATCH ~"~ ~%bgse_script%~) < 0)
        AND (INDEX (EXACT_MATCH ~\~ ~%bgse_script%~) < 0) BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT talk_line ~  !EEex_LuaTrigger("return BGSE_TalkHold and BGSE_TalkHold(EEex_LuaTrigger_Object,'','%bgse_script%') or false")~
      // First every block is counted, and those that talk on sight; only a script of nothing else is changed.
      SET count = 0
      SET talking = 0
      SET pos = 0
      WHILE (pos >= 0) BEGIN
        SET stop = 0 - 1
        SET start = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^IF%LNL%~ pos)
        PATCH_IF (start >= 0) BEGIN
          SET end = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%END%LNL%~ start)
          PATCH_IF (end >= 0) BEGIN
            SET stop = end + 5
          END
        END
        PATCH_IF (stop < 0) BEGIN
          SET pos = 0 - 1
        END ELSE BEGIN
          SET pos = stop
          READ_ASCII start block (stop - start)
          SET count += 1
          LPF bgse_talk_block INT_VAR bgse_own = bgse_own STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%block%~ RET bgse_talk END
          SET talking += bgse_talk
        END
      END
      PATCH_IF (talking > 0) AND ((talking = count) OR (bgse_own = 1)) BEGIN
        SET pos = 0
        WHILE (pos >= 0) BEGIN
          SET stop = 0 - 1
          SET start = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^IF%LNL%~ pos)
          PATCH_IF (start >= 0) BEGIN
            SET end = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%END%LNL%~ start)
            PATCH_IF (end >= 0) BEGIN
              SET stop = end + 5
            END
          END
          PATCH_IF (stop < 0) BEGIN
            SET pos = 0 - 1
          END ELSE BEGIN
            READ_ASCII start block (stop - start)
            LPF bgse_talk_block INT_VAR bgse_own = bgse_own STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%block%~ RET bgse_talk END
            PATCH_IF (bgse_talk = 1) BEGIN
              LPF bgse_aside INT_VAR bgse_from = start bgse_to = stop STR_VAR bgse_lines = EVAL ~%talk_line%~ END
              SET pos = stop + STRING_LENGTH ~%LNL%%talk_line%~
              SET bgse_talks += 1
            END ELSE BEGIN
              SET pos = stop
            END
          END
        END
        // Before the first block goes the engine's own, which queues what the fight's designer adds to the
        // creature's preparation (tools/hook_rule.py: talk_extras_block).
        TEXT_SPRINT extras_block ~IF%LNL%  See([PC])%LNL%  NumTimesTalkedTo(0)%LNL%  EEex_LuaTrigger("return BGSE_TalkExtras and BGSE_TalkExtras(EEex_LuaTrigger_Object,'','%bgse_script%') or false")%LNL%THEN%LNL%  RESPONSE #100%LNL%    EEex_LuaAction("if BGSE_TalkAct then BGSE_TalkAct(EEex_LuaAction_Object) end")%LNL%END%LNL%%LNL%~
        SET first = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^IF%LNL%~)
        INSERT_BYTES first (STRING_LENGTH ~%extras_block%~)
        WRITE_ASCIIE first ~%extras_block%~
      END
    END
  END
END

// SCS's talk on sight in the BCS in the patch buffer (bgse_talk_baf); bgse_script is its resref in lower case,
// bgse_own as there. A script that fails to decompile, patch or compile is left exactly as it was (bgse_talks 0).
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_talk_bcs
  INT_VAR bgse_own = 0
  STR_VAR bgse_script = ~~
  RET bgse_talks
BEGIN
  SET bgse_talks = 0
  READ_ASCII 0 bcs (BUFFER_LENGTH)
  PATCH_TRY
    INNER_PATCH_SAVE baf ~%bcs%~ BEGIN
      DECOMPILE_BCS_TO_BAF
    END
    LPF bgse_talk_baf INT_VAR bgse_own = bgse_own STR_VAR bgse_baf = EVAL ~%baf%~ bgse_script = EVAL ~%bgse_script%~
      RET bgse_talks bgse_baf END
    PATCH_IF (bgse_talks > 0) BEGIN
      DELETE_BYTES 0 BUFFER_LENGTH
      INSERT_BYTES 0 (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_baf%~)
      WRITE_ASCIIE 0 ~%bgse_baf%~
      COMPILE_BAF_TO_BCS
    END
  WITH DEFAULT
    SET bgse_talks = 0
    DELETE_BYTES 0 BUFFER_LENGTH
    INSERT_BYTES 0 (STRING_LENGTH ~%bcs%~)
    WRITE_ASCIIE 0 ~%bcs%~
  END
END

// How often SCS gives a block's free invisibility (tools/hook_rule.py: frequency). When SCS counts its
// uses, bgse_charges is their number (a GlobalLT counter the block raises by one: its limit; a variable
// it checks for 0 and sets above 0: one) and bgse_recharge 0; else bgse_charges is 0 and bgse_recharge
// the seconds of the block's own timer (one it checks for having run out and sets again, not the round
// timer castspell), at most 1295, or a round (6). A timer's value is a number or a name of the game's
// GTIMES.IDS (bgse_times, |NAME=SECONDS| entries in upper case; the last one of a name counts). Comments
// go first.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_frequency
  STR_VAR bgse_block = ~~
          bgse_times = ~|~
  RET bgse_charges bgse_recharge
BEGIN
  SET bgse_charges = 0
  SET bgse_recharge = 0
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE text ~%bgse_block%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~ *//.*$~ ~~
  END
  TEXT_SPRINT trig ~~
  TEXT_SPRINT resp ~~
  INNER_PATCH ~%text%~ BEGIN
    SET then = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~)
    PATCH_IF (then > 0) BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0 trig (then)
      READ_ASCII then resp (BUFFER_LENGTH - then)
    END
  END
  // A counter of its uses: the first GlobalLT whose variable the block raises by one.
  TEXT_SPRINT raised ~|~
  INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    IncrementGlobal("\([^"]+\)","LOCALS",1) *$~ BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH1%~
      TO_LOWER name
      TEXT_SPRINT raised ~%raised%%name%|~
    END ~%MATCH0%~
  END
  INNER_PATCH ~%trig%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^ +GlobalLT("\([^"]+\)","LOCALS",\([0-9]+\)) *$~ BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH1%~
      TO_LOWER name
      SET limit = MATCH2
      PATCH_IF (bgse_charges = 0) AND (limit > 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%|~ ~%raised%~) >= 0) BEGIN
        SET bgse_charges = limit
      END
    END ~%MATCH0%~
  END
  // A variable it checks for 0 and then sets: once.
  PATCH_IF (bgse_charges = 0) BEGIN
    TEXT_SPRINT sets ~|~
    INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    SetGlobal("\([^"]+\)","LOCALS",\([0-9]+\)) *$~ BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH1%~
        TO_LOWER name
        SET value = MATCH2
        PATCH_IF (value > 0) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT sets ~%sets%%name%|~
        END
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
    INNER_PATCH ~%trig%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^ +\(!GlobalGT\|Global\)("\([^"]+\)","LOCALS",0) *$~ BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH2%~
        TO_LOWER name
        PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%|~ ~%sets%~) >= 0) BEGIN
          SET bgse_charges = 1
        END
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
  END
  // Else its own timer, the first one it checks that it sets, with its first value; else a round.
  PATCH_IF (bgse_charges = 0) BEGIN
    TEXT_SPRINT timers ~|~
    INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    SetGlobalTimer("\([^"]+\)","LOCALS",\([A-Za-z0-9_]+\)) *$~ BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH1%~
        TO_LOWER name
        PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%=~ ~%timers%~) < 0) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT timers ~%timers%%name%=%MATCH2%|~
        END
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
    INNER_PATCH ~%trig%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^ +\(!GlobalTimerNotExpired\|GlobalTimerExpired\)("\([^"]+\)","LOCALS") *$~ BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH2%~
        TO_LOWER name
        SET p = INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%=~ ~%timers%~)
        PATCH_IF (bgse_recharge = 0) AND (p >= 0) AND NOT (~%name%~ STRING_EQUAL ~castspell~) BEGIN
          SET from = p + STRING_LENGTH ~|%name%=~
          INNER_PATCH ~%timers%~ BEGIN
            SET to = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|~ from)
            READ_ASCII from value (to - from)
          END
          SET seconds = 0
          PATCH_IF ((~%value%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^[0-9]+$~) = 0) BEGIN
            SET seconds = value
          END ELSE BEGIN
            TEXT_SPRINT key ~%value%~
            TO_UPPER key
            SET q = RINDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%key%=~ ~%bgse_times%~)
            PATCH_IF (q >= 0) BEGIN
              SET from = q + STRING_LENGTH ~|%key%=~
              INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_times%~ BEGIN
                SET to = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|~ from)
                READ_ASCII from number (to - from)
              END
              SET seconds = number
            END
          END
          PATCH_IF (seconds > 0) BEGIN
            SET bgse_recharge = (seconds > 1295) ? 1295 : seconds
          END
        END
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
    PATCH_IF (bgse_recharge = 0) BEGIN
      SET bgse_recharge = 6
    END
  END
END

// The real abilities that stand in for the free invisibility of a block bgse_hide_block says gives it
// (tools/hook_rule.py: gifts), each once in the block's order, as |FORM:SPELL:KIND:CHARGES:RECHARGE|
// entries: every spell the block casts or applies at the creature itself without a spellbook (FORM R
// for a resref, I for a SPELL.IDS name or number; SPELL in upper case as written), an invisibility that
// is no innate ability as the game's own of its kind (Invisibility SPWI206 or Improved Invisibility
// SPWI405, by resref). KIND is plain or improved for an invisibility (bgse_invisible, bgse_improved as
// in bgse_hide_block), else -; bgse_innate lists the spells whose files say innate (|NAME| entries in
// upper case as written); CHARGES and RECHARGE are as bgse_frequency gives them (bgse_times), - for none.
// The same gift written another way counts once. Comments go first.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_block_gifts
  STR_VAR bgse_block = ~~
          bgse_invisible = ~|~
          bgse_improved = ~|~
          bgse_innate = ~|~
          bgse_times = ~|~
  RET bgse_gifts
BEGIN
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_gifts ~|~
  LPF bgse_frequency STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%bgse_block%~ bgse_times = EVAL ~%bgse_times%~
    RET bgse_charges bgse_recharge END
  TEXT_SPRINT charges ~-~
  TEXT_SPRINT recharge ~-~
  PATCH_IF (bgse_charges > 0) BEGIN
    TEXT_SPRINT charges ~%bgse_charges%~
  END
  PATCH_IF (bgse_recharge > 0) BEGIN
    TEXT_SPRINT recharge ~%bgse_recharge%~
  END
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE text ~%bgse_block%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~ *//.*$~ ~~
  END
  INNER_PATCH ~%text%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(.*$~ BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT line ~%MATCH0%~
      TEXT_SPRINT form ~~
      TEXT_SPRINT name ~~
      PATCH_IF ((~%line%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^    \(ApplySpellRES\|ForceSpellRES\|ReallyForceSpellRES\|SpellNoDecRES\)("[^"]*",Myself) *$~) = 0) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT form ~R~
        INNER_PATCH ~%line%~ BEGIN
          REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~"\([^"]*\)"~ BEGIN
            TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH1%~
          END ~%MATCH0%~
        END
      END ELSE PATCH_IF ((~%line%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^    \(ApplySpell\|ForceSpell\|ReallyForceSpell\|SpellNoDec\)(Myself,[^,()" ]+) *$~) = 0) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT form ~I~
        INNER_PATCH ~%line%~ BEGIN
          REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~(Myself,\([^,()" ]+\))~ BEGIN
            TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH1%~
          END ~%MATCH0%~
        END
      END
      PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%name%~ > 0) BEGIN
        TO_UPPER name
        TEXT_SPRINT kind ~-~
        PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%|~ ~%bgse_improved%~) >= 0) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT kind ~improved~
        END ELSE PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%|~ ~%bgse_invisible%~) >= 0) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT kind ~plain~
        END
        PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%kind%~ > 1) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%|~ ~%bgse_innate%~) < 0) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT form ~R~
          TEXT_SPRINT name ~SPWI206~
          PATCH_IF (~%kind%~ STRING_EQUAL ~improved~) BEGIN
            TEXT_SPRINT name ~SPWI405~
          END
        END
        PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~:%name%:%kind%:%charges%:%recharge%|~ ~%bgse_gifts%~) < 0) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT bgse_gifts ~%bgse_gifts%%form%:%name%:%kind%:%charges%:%recharge%|~
        END
      END
    END ~%MATCH0%~
  END
END

// The name of the innate copy of a spell (bgse_res, a resref) that comes back bgse_recharge seconds
// after each use, 0 for never (tools/hook_rule.py: gift_name): BG, the spell's tag (W, P, N or C and
// its number for SPWI, SPPR, SPIN and SPCL spells, else the first four characters of its resref) and
// the recharge, at most 1295 seconds, as two base-36 digits.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_gift_name
  INT_VAR bgse_recharge = 0
  STR_VAR bgse_res = ~~
  RET bgse_name
BEGIN
  TEXT_SPRINT res ~%bgse_res%~
  TO_UPPER res
  PATCH_IF ((~%res%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^SP\(WI\|PR\|IN\|CL\)[0-9][0-9][0-9]$~) = 0) BEGIN
    INNER_PATCH ~%res%~ BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 2 kind (2)
      READ_ASCII 4 number (3)
    END
    TEXT_SPRINT tag ~C%number%~
    PATCH_IF (~%kind%~ STRING_EQUAL ~WI~) BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT tag ~W%number%~
    END ELSE PATCH_IF (~%kind%~ STRING_EQUAL ~PR~) BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT tag ~P%number%~
    END ELSE PATCH_IF (~%kind%~ STRING_EQUAL ~IN~) BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT tag ~N%number%~
    END
  END ELSE PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%res%~ > 4) BEGIN
    INNER_PATCH ~%res%~ BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0 tag (4)
    END
  END ELSE BEGIN
    TEXT_SPRINT tag ~%res%~
  END
  SET r = (bgse_recharge < 0) ? 0 : ((bgse_recharge > 1295) ? 1295 : bgse_recharge)
  INNER_PATCH ~0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ~ BEGIN
    READ_ASCII (r / 36) high (1)
    READ_ASCII (r - (r / 36) * 36) low (1)
  END
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_name ~BG%tag%%high%%low%~
END

// A block's scripted teleports (tools/hook_rule.py: scripted_teleports, is_jump): how many casts
// without a spellbook check cast a spell that moves the caster (bgse_teleports, |NAME| entries in
// upper case), and whether one of them is a jump into the fight: at an enemy, a party member or
// the creature last seen, which a trigger says the creature sees or detects, unless the creature
// must be on the party's side. Comments go first.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_block_teleports
  STR_VAR bgse_block = ~~
          bgse_teleports = ~|~
  RET bgse_scripted bgse_jump
BEGIN
  SET bgse_scripted = 0
  SET bgse_jump = 0
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE text ~%bgse_block%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~ *//.*$~ ~~
  END
  TEXT_SPRINT trig ~~
  TEXT_SPRINT resp ~~
  INNER_PATCH ~%text%~ BEGIN
    SET then = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~)
    PATCH_IF (then > 0) BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0 trig (then)
      READ_ASCII then resp (BUFFER_LENGTH - then)
    END
  END
  PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%resp%~ > 0)
      AND ((~%trig%~ STRING_CONTAINS_REGEXP ~[^A-Za-z0-9_]\(HaveSpell\|HaveSpellRES\|HasItem\|KnowSpell\)(~) != 0) BEGIN
    SET ally = (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^ +Allegiance(Myself,GOODCUTOFF)~ ~%trig%~) >= 0) ? 1 : 0
    TEXT_SPRINT seen ~|~
    INNER_PATCH ~%trig%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^ +\(See\|Detect\)(\(.*\)) *$~ BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT seen ~%seen%%MATCH2%|~
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
    INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    \(ReallyForceSpellPointRES\|ReallyForceSpellPoint\|ReallyForceSpellRES\|ReallyForceSpell\|ForceSpellPointRES\|ForceSpellPoint\|ForceSpellRES\|ForceSpell\)(\(.*\)) *$~ BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT action ~%MATCH1%~
        TEXT_SPRINT args ~%MATCH2%~
        LPF bgse_cast_parts STR_VAR bgse_action = EVAL ~%action%~ bgse_args = EVAL ~%args%~ RET bgse_spell bgse_target END
        PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%bgse_spell%|~ ~%bgse_teleports%~) >= 0) BEGIN
          SET bgse_scripted += 1
          PATCH_IF (ally = 0) AND (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_target%~ > 0)
              AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%bgse_target%|~ ~%seen%~) >= 0)
              AND ((~%bgse_target%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^\(Player[1-6]\|NearestEnemyOf(Myself)\|LastSeenBy(Myself)\|\[\(PC\|GOODCUTOFF\|ENEMY\|ANYONE\)[^]]*\]\)$~) = 0) BEGIN
            SET bgse_jump = 1
          END
        END
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
  END
END

// Number of action lines in a response part that are not part of an ordinary combat round
// (tools/hook_rule.py: COMBAT).
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_foreign_actions
  STR_VAR bgse_resp = ~~
  RET bgse_foreign
BEGIN
  SET bgse_foreign = 0
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE rest ~%bgse_resp%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    \(ForceSpell\|ForceSpellRES\|ReallyForceSpell\|ReallyForceSpellRES\|ForceSpellPoint\|ForceSpellPointRES\|ReallyForceSpellPoint\|ReallyForceSpellPointRES\|Spell\|SpellRES\|SpellNoDec\|SpellNoDecRES\|SpellPoint\|SpellPointRES\|UseItem\|Attack\|AttackOneRound\|AttackReevaluate\|AttackNoSound\|EquipMostDamagingMelee\|EquipRanged\|SelectWeaponAbility\|MoveToObject\|RunAwayFrom\|RunAwayFromNoLeaveArea\|RunAwayFromNoInterrupt\|RunAwayFromNoInterruptNoLeaveArea\|RandomWalk\|RandomWalkContinuous\|FaceObject\|Turn\|OpenDoor\|Wait\|SmallWait\|NoAction\|SetInterrupt\|ClearActions\|RemoveSpell\|ApplySpellRES\|ApplySpell\|Continue\|SetGlobal\|SetGlobalTimer\|SetGlobalTimerRandom\|IncrementGlobal\|DisplayString\|DisplayStringHead\|VerbalConstant\|PlaySound\)(.*$~ ~~
  END
  INNER_PATCH ~%rest%~ BEGIN
    COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(~ bgse_foreign
  END
END

// Flags for one block (BAF text with \n line ends, from its IF line to its END line), as bits of
// bgse_flags: 1 book, 2 items, 4 special, 8 pick, 16 lastseen and 32 encounter, each only where it
// decides: items only for bookkeeping (a run of it carries them), lastseen only for a special or an
// encounter (it aims at the target picks before it). bgse_anchor is 1 for the anchor, looked for only
// when bgse_seek is 1.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_classify_block
  INT_VAR bgse_seek = 1
  STR_VAR bgse_block = ~~
  RET bgse_anchor bgse_flags
BEGIN
  SET bgse_anchor = 0
  SET bgse_flags = 0
  TEXT_SPRINT trig ~~
  TEXT_SPRINT resp ~~
  INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_block%~ BEGIN
    SET then = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~)
    PATCH_IF (then > 0) BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0 trig (then)
      READ_ASCII then resp (BUFFER_LENGTH - then)
    END
  END
  PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%resp%~ > 0) BEGIN
    SET responses = 0
    SET ends_continue = 0
    SET only_continue = 0
    TEXT_SPRINT parts ~~
    INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
      // Each response, whether its last action is Continue() and whether that is its only one
      // (action names compare in any case); without a Continue() no response ends with one.
      SET pos = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%  RESPONSE #~)
      PATCH_IF (pos >= 0) BEGIN
        READ_ASCII pos parts (BUFFER_LENGTH - pos)
      END
      SET continues = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_INSENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~    Continue(~)
      WHILE (pos >= 0) BEGIN
        SET next = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%  RESPONSE #~ (pos + 1))
        SET responses += 1
        PATCH_IF (continues >= 0) BEGIN
          SET last = RINDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(~ ((next >= 0) ? next : BUFFER_LENGTH))
          PATCH_IF (last > pos) BEGIN
            PATCH_IF (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_INSENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~    Continue(~ last) = last) BEGIN
              SET ends_continue += 1
              PATCH_IF (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(~ pos) = last) BEGIN
                SET only_continue += 1
              END
            END
          END
        END
        SET pos = next
      END
    END
    // The actions of the responses go by kind, as above, each counted only where it decides. The
    // anchor checks the round timer, is no first-round cast and no retarget alone (only SetGlobal,
    // SetGlobalTimer, IncrementGlobal and ClearActions, with a ClearActions).
    PATCH_IF (bgse_seek = 1) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~GlobalTimerNotExpired("castspell","LOCALS")~ ~%trig%~) >= 0)
         AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~SetGlobal("instantprep","LOCALS",1)~ ~%resp%~) < 0) BEGIN
      INNER_PATCH ~%parts%~ BEGIN
        COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(~ all
        COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_INSENSITIVE ~^    \(SetGlobal\|SetGlobalTimer\|IncrementGlobal\|ClearActions\)(~ retargets
        COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_INSENSITIVE ~^    ClearActions(~ clears
      END
      PATCH_IF NOT ((all = retargets) AND (clears > 0)) BEGIN
        SET bgse_anchor = 1
      END
    END
    // Bookkeeping: every response ends with Continue(), the only actions beyond SetGlobal,
    // SetGlobalTimer, IncrementGlobal, Continue, DisplayString, DisplayStringHead and items are its
    // ApplySpellRES at itself, and no trigger perceives anyone. It carries items or what it applies.
    PATCH_IF (responses > 0) AND (ends_continue = responses) BEGIN
      INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
        COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    ApplySpellRES("[^"]*",Myself)~ self_applies
      END
      INNER_PATCH ~%parts%~ BEGIN
        COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(~ all
        COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_INSENSITIVE ~^    \(SetGlobal\|SetGlobalTimer\|IncrementGlobal\|Continue\|DisplayString\|DisplayStringHead\|GiveItemCreate\|DestroyItem\|CreateItem\)(~ booked
        COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_INSENSITIVE ~^    ApplySpellRES(~ apply_names
      END
      PATCH_IF (all - booked = self_applies) AND (apply_names = self_applies)
          AND ((~%trig%~ STRING_CONTAINS_REGEXP ~[^A-Za-z0-9_]\(See\|Detect\|Heard\|Range\|AttackedBy\|HitBy\|LastSeenBy\|LastHeardBy\|LastAttackerOf\|LastTargetedBy\|NearestEnemyOf\|Nearest\|SecondNearest\|ThirdNearest\|InParty\|SpellCast\|SpellCastOnMe\|SpellCastPriest\|SpellCastInnate\)(\|\[\(PC\|ENEMY\|ANYONE\|GOODCUTOFF\|EVILCUTOFF\|NEUTRAL\)\|Player[1-6]~) != 0) BEGIN
        SET bgse_flags = 1
        INNER_PATCH ~%parts%~ BEGIN
          COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_INSENSITIVE ~^    \(GiveItemCreate\|DestroyItem\|CreateItem\)(~ item_names
        END
        PATCH_IF (item_names > 0) OR (self_applies > 0) BEGIN
          SET bgse_flags = bgse_flags BOR 2
        END
      END
    END
    // A cast without a spellbook check is a special. So is a SpellNoDec cast without one, unless the
    // block also removes the spell (tools/hook_rule.py: NO_DECREMENT), and a power the creature
    // applies to itself (SELF_POWER).
    PATCH_IF ((~%trig%~ STRING_CONTAINS_REGEXP ~[^A-Za-z0-9_]\(HaveSpell\|HaveSpellRES\|HasItem\|KnowSpell\)(~) != 0) BEGIN
      INNER_PATCH ~%parts%~ BEGIN
        COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_INSENSITIVE ~^    \(ForceSpell\|ForceSpellRES\|ReallyForceSpell\|ReallyForceSpellRES\|ForceSpellPoint\|ForceSpellPointRES\|ReallyForceSpellPoint\|ReallyForceSpellPointRES\)(~ ungated
        COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_INSENSITIVE ~^    \(SpellNoDec\|SpellNoDecRES\)(~ nodec
        COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_INSENSITIVE ~^    RemoveSpell(~ removes
      END
      INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
        COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    \(ApplySpellRES("[^"]*",Myself)\|ApplySpell(Myself,\)~ self_powers
      END
      PATCH_IF (ungated > 0) OR ((nodec > 0) AND (removes = 0)) OR (self_powers > 0) BEGIN
        SET bgse_flags = bgse_flags BOR 4
      END
    END
    PATCH_IF (responses > 0) AND (only_continue = responses) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~See(~ ~%trig%~) >= 0) BEGIN
      SET bgse_flags = bgse_flags BOR 8
    END
    PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~Die()~ ~%trig%~) >= 0) BEGIN
      SET bgse_flags = bgse_flags BOR 32
    END ELSE BEGIN
      LPF bgse_foreign_actions STR_VAR bgse_resp = EVAL ~%resp%~ RET bgse_foreign END
      PATCH_IF (bgse_foreign > 0) BEGIN
        SET bgse_flags = bgse_flags BOR 32
      END
    END
    PATCH_IF ((bgse_flags BAND 36) > 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~LastSeenBy(Myself)~ ~%bgse_block%~) >= 0) BEGIN
      SET bgse_flags = bgse_flags BOR 16
    END
  END
END

// Whether a block pursues a creature the creature does not perceive (tools/hook_rule.py:
// is_pursuit): its triggers say it sees or detects no enemy (the nearest enemy or a whole class
// of creatures), or not the one it acts on, and a response walks, jumps, casts, uses an item or
// attacks at a party member, the nearest enemy, the creature last seen or a class of creatures
// that no trigger says it sees or detects; not when the creature must be on the party's side. Or
// it random-walks while an unseen attacker puzzles it (the whatthe timer) and sees or detects no
// enemy. Comments go first.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_pursuit_block
  STR_VAR bgse_block = ~~
  RET bgse_pursuit
BEGIN
  SET bgse_pursuit = 0
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE text ~%bgse_block%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~ *//.*$~ ~~
  END
  TEXT_SPRINT trig ~~
  TEXT_SPRINT resp ~~
  INNER_PATCH ~%text%~ BEGIN
    SET then = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~)
    PATCH_IF (then > 0) BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0 trig (then)
      READ_ASCII then resp (BUFFER_LENGTH - then)
    END
  END
  PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%resp%~ > 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^ +Allegiance(Myself,GOODCUTOFF)~ ~%trig%~) < 0) BEGIN
    // The creatures the triggers say it sees or detects and those they say it does not, as
    // |object| lists; not seeing the nearest enemy or a whole class means no enemy.
    TEXT_SPRINT seen ~|~
    TEXT_SPRINT unseen ~|~
    SET none_seen = 0
    INNER_PATCH ~%trig%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^ +\(!?\)\(See\|Detect\)(\(.*\)) *$~ BEGIN
        PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%MATCH1%~ > 0) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT unseen ~%unseen%%MATCH3%|~
          PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^\(NearestEnemyOf(Myself)\|\[\(PC\|GOODCUTOFF\|ENEMY\|ANYONE\)\]\)$~ ~%MATCH3%~) = 0) BEGIN
            SET none_seen = 1
          END
        END ELSE BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT seen ~%seen%%MATCH3%|~
        END
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
    PATCH_IF (none_seen = 1) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^ +GlobalTimerNotExpired("whatthe","LOCALS")~ ~%trig%~) >= 0)
        AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    RandomWalk\(Continuous\)?(~ ~%resp%~) >= 0) BEGIN
      SET bgse_pursuit = 1
    END ELSE BEGIN
      // The objects of its walks, jumps, casts, item uses and attacks, one action a line.
      TEXT_SPRINT args ~~
      INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
        REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    \(MoveToObject\|MoveToObjectFollow\|MoveToObjectNoInterrupt\|JumpToObject\|ForceSpell\|ForceSpellRES\|ReallyForceSpell\|ReallyForceSpellRES\|Spell\|SpellRES\|SpellNoDec\|SpellNoDecRES\|UseItem\|Attack\|AttackOneRound\|AttackReevaluate\|AttackNoSound\)(\(.*\)) *$~ BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT args ~%args%%MATCH2%%LNL%~
        END ~%MATCH0%~
      END
      INNER_PATCH ~%args%~ BEGIN
        REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~Player[1-6]\|NearestEnemyOf(Myself)\|LastSeenBy(Myself)\|\[\(PC\|GOODCUTOFF\|ENEMY\|ANYONE\)[^]]*\]~ BEGIN
          PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%MATCH0%|~ ~%seen%~) < 0)
              AND ((none_seen = 1) OR (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%MATCH0%|~ ~%unseen%~) >= 0)) BEGIN
            SET bgse_pursuit = 1
          END
        END ~%MATCH0%~
      END
    END
  END
END

// Whether a block belongs to SCS's hunt for enemies the creature cannot see (tools/hook_rule.py:
// is_hunt): it walks to the nearest door and opens it, casts on its detect timer, uses SCS's
// chase variables for more than bookkeeping that ends with Continue(), or pursues a creature it
// does not perceive (bgse_pursuit_block).
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_hunt_block
  STR_VAR bgse_block = ~~
  RET bgse_hunt
BEGIN
  SET bgse_hunt = 0
  TEXT_SPRINT resp ~~
  INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_block%~ BEGIN
    SET then = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~)
    PATCH_IF (then > 0) BEGIN
      READ_ASCII then resp (BUFFER_LENGTH - then)
    END
  END
  PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%resp%~ > 0) BEGIN
    // Responses, those whose last action is Continue(), and actions beyond the chase's
    // bookkeeping (tools/hook_rule.py: HUNT_BOOKKEEPING).
    SET responses = 0
    SET ends_continue = 0
    TEXT_SPRINT parts ~~
    INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
      // Whether each response's last action is Continue() (action names compare in any case).
      SET pos = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%  RESPONSE #~)
      PATCH_IF (pos >= 0) BEGIN
        READ_ASCII pos parts (BUFFER_LENGTH - pos)
      END
      WHILE (pos >= 0) BEGIN
        SET next = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%  RESPONSE #~ (pos + 1))
        SET stop = (next >= 0) ? next : BUFFER_LENGTH
        SET responses += 1
        SET last = RINDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(~ stop)
        PATCH_IF (last > pos) BEGIN
          PATCH_IF (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_INSENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~    Continue(~ last) = last) BEGIN
            SET ends_continue += 1
          END
        END
        SET pos = next
      END
    END
    // The actions of the responses beyond the bookkeeping, as above.
    INNER_PATCH ~%parts%~ BEGIN
      COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(~ all
      COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_INSENSITIVE ~^    \(SetGlobal\|SetGlobalTimer\|SetGlobalTimerRandom\|IncrementGlobal\|Continue\|DisplayString\|DisplayStringHead\)(~ booked
    END
    SET acts = all - booked
    PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%    OpenDoor(NearestDoor)~ ~%resp%~) >= 0)
        OR ((acts > 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_INSENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%    SetGlobalTimer("detect","LOCALS",~ ~%resp%~) >= 0)) BEGIN
      SET bgse_hunt = 1
    END ELSE PATCH_IF (acts > 0) OR (ends_continue < responses) BEGIN
      PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_INSENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~"chasetimer","LOCALS"~ ~%bgse_block%~) >= 0)
          OR (INDEX (CASE_INSENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~"chasing","LOCALS"~ ~%bgse_block%~) >= 0)
          OR (INDEX (CASE_INSENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~"chasepc","LOCALS"~ ~%bgse_block%~) >= 0)
          OR (INDEX (CASE_INSENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~"chasetarget","LOCALS"~ ~%bgse_block%~) >= 0)
          OR (INDEX (CASE_INSENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~"teleportpursuetimer","LOCALS"~ ~%bgse_block%~) >= 0) BEGIN
        SET bgse_hunt = 1
      END
    END
  END
  PATCH_IF (bgse_hunt = 0) BEGIN
    LPF bgse_pursuit_block STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%bgse_block%~ RET bgse_pursuit END
    SET bgse_hunt = bgse_pursuit
  END
END

// Whom a block walks its creature to while it perceives no enemy, as the script names it, or empty
// (tools/hook_rule.py: party_walk). A party member (Player1 to Player6 or [PC]): the block is a pursuit
// (bgse_pursuit_block) and a response walks there (MoveToObject, MoveToObjectFollow or MoveToObjectNoInterrupt);
// the first such walk. Or the creature it heard (LastHeardBy(Myself)), the answer to a call for help: the
// triggers say it sees or detects no enemy, and the responses hold nothing but such walks and Continue().
// Comments go first.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_party_walk
  STR_VAR bgse_block = ~~
  RET bgse_target
BEGIN
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_target ~~
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE text ~%bgse_block%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~ *//.*$~ ~~
  END
  LPF bgse_pursuit_block STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%bgse_block%~ RET bgse_pursuit END
  PATCH_IF (bgse_pursuit = 1) BEGIN
    INNER_PATCH ~%text%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    \(MoveToObject\|MoveToObjectFollow\|MoveToObjectNoInterrupt\)(\(Player[1-6]\|\[PC\]\)) *$~ BEGIN
        PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_target%~ = 0) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT bgse_target ~%MATCH2%~
        END
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
  END
  PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_target%~ = 0) BEGIN
    SET then = INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~ ~%text%~)
    PATCH_IF (then > 0) BEGIN
      INNER_PATCH ~%text%~ BEGIN
        READ_ASCII 0 trig (then)
        READ_ASCII then resp (BUFFER_LENGTH - then)
      END
      PATCH_IF ((~%trig%~ STRING_CONTAINS_REGEXP ~%LNL% +!\(See\|Detect\)(NearestEnemyOf(Myself))~) = 0) BEGIN
        SET heard = 0
        SET acts = 0
        SET goes_on = 0
        INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
          COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    \(MoveToObject\|MoveToObjectFollow\|MoveToObjectNoInterrupt\)(LastHeardBy(Myself)) *$~ heard
          COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(~ acts
          COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    Continue() *$~ goes_on
        END
        PATCH_IF (heard > 0) AND (acts = heard + goes_on) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT bgse_target ~LastHeardBy(Myself)~
        END
      END
    END
  END
END

// Walks at party members in one decompiled script that the SCS rule did not hook (tools/hook_rule.py:
// patch_hunt; Christopher, 2026-11-10: SCS's ambushes are taken over as they are for now, the groups come
// straight at the party). bgse_script is its resref in lower case. Each block that walks its creature to a party
// member it does not perceive (bgse_party_walk) gets a last condition that holds when BGSE_Hunt says no, with no
// family and naming that member: BGSE_Hunt goes by the script that decides for the creature (kernel/hook.lua,
// driver), and the engine's search goes for that member itself. bgse_walks counts them. A script the SCS rule
// hooked (BGSE_Claim in it), one patched before (BGSE_Hunt in it) and one whose name cannot go into Lua text stay
// as they are. bgse_baf comes back without carriage returns, as bgse_hook_baf gives it.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_hunt_baf
  STR_VAR bgse_baf = ~~
          bgse_script = ~~
  RET bgse_walks bgse_baf
BEGIN
  SET bgse_walks = 0
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE bgse_baf ~%bgse_baf%~ BEGIN
    PATCH_IF (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%MNL%~) >= 0) BEGIN
      REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%MNL%~ ~~
    END
    PATCH_IF (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~BGSE_Claim~) < 0) AND (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~BGSE_Hunt~) < 0)
        AND (INDEX (EXACT_MATCH ~'~ ~%bgse_script%~) < 0) AND (INDEX (EXACT_MATCH ~"~ ~%bgse_script%~) < 0)
        AND (INDEX (EXACT_MATCH ~\~ ~%bgse_script%~) < 0) BEGIN
      SET pos = 0
      WHILE (pos >= 0) BEGIN
        SET stop = 0 - 1
        SET start = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^IF%LNL%~ pos)
        PATCH_IF (start >= 0) BEGIN
          SET end = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%END%LNL%~ start)
          PATCH_IF (end >= 0) BEGIN
            SET stop = end + 5
          END
        END
        PATCH_IF (stop < 0) BEGIN
          SET pos = 0 - 1
        END ELSE BEGIN
          SET pos = stop
          READ_ASCII start block (stop - start)
          PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    MoveToObject~ ~%block%~) >= 0) BEGIN
            LPF bgse_party_walk STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%block%~ RET bgse_target END
            PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_target%~ > 0) BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT hunt_line ~  !EEex_LuaTrigger("return BGSE_Hunt and BGSE_Hunt(EEex_LuaTrigger_Object,'','%bgse_script%','%bgse_target%') or false")~
              LPF bgse_aside INT_VAR bgse_from = start bgse_to = stop STR_VAR bgse_lines = EVAL ~%hunt_line%~ END
              SET pos = stop + STRING_LENGTH ~%LNL%%hunt_line%~
              SET bgse_walks += 1
            END
          END
        END
      END
    END
  END
END

// The compiled forms a script with such a walk holds (setup-bgse.tp2 decompiles only those; bgse_exit_candidate
// finds them in one block), from the game's TRIGGER.IDS and ACTION.IDS: bgse_unseen a negated See or Detect (TR,
// the trigger's number, a value and flags with the negation bit), bgse_walkto an action MoveToObject,
// MoveToObjectFollow or MoveToObjectNoInterrupt (AC and its number). Each is empty when the game has none of them.
DEFINE_ACTION_FUNCTION bgse_walk_patterns
  RET bgse_unseen bgse_walkto
BEGIN
  OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT unseen ~~
  ACTION_FOR_EACH name IN ~See~ ~Detect~ BEGIN
    OUTER_SET id = IDS_OF_SYMBOL (~TRIGGER~ ~%name%~)
    ACTION_IF (id >= 0) BEGIN
      ACTION_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%unseen%~ > 0) BEGIN
        OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT unseen ~%unseen%\|~
      END
      OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT unseen ~%unseen%%id%~
    END
  END
  OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT walkto ~~
  ACTION_FOR_EACH name IN ~MoveToObject~ ~MoveToObjectFollow~ ~MoveToObjectNoInterrupt~ BEGIN
    OUTER_SET id = IDS_OF_SYMBOL (~ACTION~ ~%name%~)
    ACTION_IF (id >= 0) BEGIN
      ACTION_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%walkto%~ > 0) BEGIN
        OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT walkto ~%walkto%\|~
      END
      OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT walkto ~%walkto%%id%~
    END
  END
  OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT bgse_unseen ~~
  OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT bgse_walkto ~~
  ACTION_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%unseen%~ > 0) AND (STRING_LENGTH ~%walkto%~ > 0) BEGIN
    OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT bgse_unseen ~TR%LNL%\(%unseen%\) [0-9]+ [0-9]*[13579] ~
    OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT bgse_walkto ~AC%LNL%\(%walkto%\)OB~
  END
END

// Walks at party members in the BCS in the patch buffer (bgse_hunt_baf); bgse_script is its resref in lower
// case. A script that fails to decompile, patch or compile is left exactly as it was (bgse_walks 0).
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_hunt_bcs
  STR_VAR bgse_script = ~~
  RET bgse_walks
BEGIN
  SET bgse_walks = 0
  READ_ASCII 0 bcs (BUFFER_LENGTH)
  PATCH_TRY
    INNER_PATCH_SAVE baf ~%bcs%~ BEGIN
      DECOMPILE_BCS_TO_BAF
    END
    LPF bgse_hunt_baf STR_VAR bgse_baf = EVAL ~%baf%~ bgse_script = EVAL ~%bgse_script%~ RET bgse_walks bgse_baf END
    PATCH_IF (bgse_walks > 0) BEGIN
      DELETE_BYTES 0 BUFFER_LENGTH
      INSERT_BYTES 0 (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_baf%~)
      WRITE_ASCIIE 0 ~%bgse_baf%~
      COMPILE_BAF_TO_BCS
    END
  WITH DEFAULT
    SET bgse_walks = 0
    DELETE_BYTES 0 BUFFER_LENGTH
    INSERT_BYTES 0 (STRING_LENGTH ~%bcs%~)
    WRITE_ASCIIE 0 ~%bcs%~
  END
END

// A spell's name as it goes into Lua text inside a BAF string (tools/hook_rule.py: token): at most 64
// letters, digits, _, # and -, as a creature's orders can name it; else empty.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_token
  STR_VAR bgse_name = ~~
  RET bgse_token
BEGIN
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_token ~~
  PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_name%~ > 0) AND (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_name%~ <= 64)
      AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^[A-Za-z0-9_#-]+$~ ~%bgse_name%~) = 0) BEGIN
    TEXT_SPRINT bgse_token ~%bgse_name%~
  END
END

// SCS's preparation (tools/hook_rule.py: prep_kind): bgse_prep is prebuff, contingency, chain or
// opener, else empty; bgse_cast names the first cast's spell and bgse_spent the first spell taken from
// the spellbook, as written (empty: none, or a name unsafe in Lua text, bgse_token). Every action is
// bookkeeping or a cast of the kind, with one cast at least. Openers cast at the creature itself
// (Spell, SpellRES, ForceSpell or ForceSpellRES) and set instantprep to 1. The others cast at once
// (ReallyForceSpell or ReallyForceSpellRES) and may take the spell from the spellbook (RemoveSpell or
// RemoveSpellRES): a chain at the creature or [PC], setting ChainContingencyFired; a contingency at the
// creature, setting ContingencyFired (either in any case); a prebuff at the creature while instantprep
// is 0 (a trigger of two spaces: not one of an OR group). Comments go first.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_prep_block
  STR_VAR bgse_block = ~~
  RET bgse_prep bgse_cast bgse_spent
BEGIN
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_prep ~~
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_cast ~~
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_spent ~~
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE text ~%bgse_block%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~ *//.*$~ ~~
  END
  TEXT_SPRINT trig ~~
  TEXT_SPRINT resp ~~
  INNER_PATCH ~%text%~ BEGIN
    SET then = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~)
    PATCH_IF (then > 0) BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0 trig (then)
      READ_ASCII then resp (BUFFER_LENGTH - then)
    END
  END
  PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%resp%~ > 0) BEGIN
    SET opener = (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~SetGlobal("instantprep","LOCALS",1)~ ~%resp%~) >= 0) ? 1 : 0
    // Casts, actions of other kinds, casts at [PC] and elsewhere than the creature itself, the fired
    // variables set, and the first cast's and the first removed spell.
    SET casts = 0
    SET foreign = 0
    SET party = 0
    SET elsewhere = 0
    SET chain = 0
    SET fired = 0
    SET spends = 0
    TEXT_SPRINT first ~~
    TEXT_SPRINT spent ~~
    INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    \([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\)(.*$~ BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT action ~%MATCH1%~
        TEXT_SPRINT line ~%MATCH0%~
        SET cast = 0
        SET spend = 0
        PATCH_IF ((~%action%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^\(SetGlobal\|SetGlobalTimer\|SetGlobalTimerRandom\|IncrementGlobal\|Continue\|DisplayString\|DisplayStringHead\)$~) = 0) BEGIN
          INNER_PATCH ~%line%~ BEGIN
            REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    SetGlobal("\([A-Za-z]+\)","LOCALS",1) *$~ BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH1%~
              TO_LOWER name
              PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%|~ ~|chaincontingencyfired|~) = 0) BEGIN
                SET chain = 1
              END ELSE PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%|~ ~|contingencyfired|~) = 0) BEGIN
                SET fired = 1
              END
            END ~%MATCH0%~
          END
        END ELSE PATCH_IF (opener = 1) AND ((~%action%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^\(Spell\|SpellRES\|ForceSpell\|ForceSpellRES\)$~) = 0) BEGIN
          SET cast = 1
        END ELSE PATCH_IF (opener = 0) AND ((~%action%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^\(ReallyForceSpell\|ReallyForceSpellRES\)$~) = 0) BEGIN
          SET cast = 1
        END ELSE PATCH_IF (opener = 0) AND ((~%action%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^\(RemoveSpell\|RemoveSpellRES\)$~) = 0) BEGIN
          SET spend = 1
        END ELSE BEGIN
          SET foreign += 1
        END
        TEXT_SPRINT args ~~
        SET parsed = 0
        PATCH_IF (cast = 1) OR ((spend = 1) AND (spends = 0)) BEGIN
          INNER_PATCH ~%line%~ BEGIN
            REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    [A-Za-z]+(\(.*\)) *$~ BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT args ~%MATCH1%~
              SET parsed = 1
            END ~%MATCH0%~
          END
        END
        PATCH_IF (parsed = 1) AND (spend = 1) BEGIN
          SET spends = 1
          INNER_PATCH_SAVE spent ~%args%~ BEGIN
            REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~^ +\| +$~ ~~
            REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~"~ ~~
          END
        END
        PATCH_IF (parsed = 1) AND (cast = 1) BEGIN
          LPF bgse_cast_parts INT_VAR bgse_upper = 0 STR_VAR bgse_action = EVAL ~%action%~ bgse_args = EVAL ~%args%~
            RET bgse_spell bgse_target END
          INNER_PATCH_SAVE bgse_spell ~%bgse_spell%~ BEGIN
            REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~^ +\| +$~ ~~
          END
          INNER_PATCH_SAVE bgse_target ~%bgse_target%~ BEGIN
            REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~^ +\| +$~ ~~
          END
          SET casts += 1
          PATCH_IF (casts = 1) BEGIN
            TEXT_SPRINT first ~%bgse_spell%~
          END
          PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%bgse_target%|~ ~|[PC]|~) = 0) BEGIN
            SET party += 1
          END ELSE PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%bgse_target%|~ ~|Myself|~) < 0) BEGIN
            SET elsewhere += 1
          END
        END
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
    PATCH_IF (casts > 0) AND (foreign = 0) AND (elsewhere = 0) BEGIN
      PATCH_IF (opener = 1) BEGIN
        PATCH_IF (party = 0) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT bgse_prep ~opener~
        END
      END ELSE PATCH_IF (chain = 1) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT bgse_prep ~chain~
      END ELSE PATCH_IF (fired = 1) BEGIN
        PATCH_IF (party = 0) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT bgse_prep ~contingency~
        END
      END ELSE PATCH_IF (party = 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^  Global("instantprep","LOCALS",0) *$~ ~%trig%~) >= 0) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT bgse_prep ~prebuff~
      END
    END
    PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_prep%~ > 0) BEGIN
      LPF bgse_token STR_VAR bgse_name = EVAL ~%first%~ RET bgse_token END
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_cast ~%bgse_token%~
      LPF bgse_token STR_VAR bgse_name = EVAL ~%spent%~ RET bgse_token END
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_spent ~%bgse_token%~
    END
  END
END

// Add trigger lines (bgse_lines) to the block from bgse_from to bgse_to in the patch buffer:
// last, or first when its triggers end inside their last OR(n) group with fewer than n lines
// after it, which the lines would otherwise join (tools/hook_rule.py: aside).
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_aside
  INT_VAR bgse_from = 0
          bgse_to = 0
  STR_VAR bgse_lines = ~~
BEGIN
  READ_ASCII bgse_from block (bgse_to - bgse_from)
  SET then = INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~ ~%block%~)
  TEXT_SPRINT trig ~~
  INNER_PATCH ~%block%~ BEGIN
    READ_ASCII 0 trig (then)
  END
  SET or_open = 0
  INNER_PATCH ~%trig%~ BEGIN
    SET or_last = RINDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~%LNL% +OR(~)
    PATCH_IF (or_last >= 0) BEGIN
      READ_ASCII (or_last + 1) or_rest (BUFFER_LENGTH - or_last - 1)
      SET or_want = 0
      SET or_lines = 0
      INNER_PATCH ~%or_rest%~ BEGIN
        REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^ +OR(\([0-9]+\))~ BEGIN
          SET or_want = MATCH1
        END ~%MATCH0%~
        COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%~ or_lines
      END
      SET or_open = (or_lines < or_want) ? 1 : 0
    END
  END
  PATCH_IF (or_open = 1) BEGIN
    INSERT_BYTES (bgse_from + 3) (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_lines%%LNL%~)
    WRITE_ASCIIE (bgse_from + 3) ~%bgse_lines%%LNL%~
  END ELSE BEGIN
    INSERT_BYTES (bgse_from + then) (STRING_LENGTH ~%LNL%%bgse_lines%~)
    WRITE_ASCIIE (bgse_from + then) ~%LNL%%bgse_lines%~
  END
END

// Add an action (bgse_notice) as the last of each response that casts at once (ReallyForceSpell or
// ReallyForceSpellRES) of the block that starts at bgse_from in the patch buffer, before the response's
// closing Continue(), which stays last (tools/hook_rule.py: notify). Comments do not count.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_notify
  INT_VAR bgse_from = 0
  STR_VAR bgse_notice = ~~
BEGIN
  SET then = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~ bgse_from)
  SET stop = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%END%LNL%~ bgse_from)
  // From the last response up, so the ones before keep their offsets; a response runs from the line
  // end before its RESPONSE line to the line end before the next one or the block's END.
  SET pos = RINDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%  RESPONSE #~ stop)
  WHILE (pos > then) BEGIN
    READ_ASCII pos chunk (stop - pos)
    INNER_PATCH_SAVE clean ~%chunk%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~ *//.*$~ ~~
    END
    PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    ReallyForceSpell\(RES\)?(.*) *$~ ~%clean%~) >= 0) BEGIN
      // Its last action line.
      SET last = 0 - 1
      SET eol = 0
      TEXT_SPRINT line ~~
      INNER_PATCH ~%chunk%~ BEGIN
        SET last = RINDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~%LNL%    [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(~)
        PATCH_IF (last >= 0) BEGIN
          SET eol = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%~ (last + 1))
          PATCH_IF (eol < 0) BEGIN
            SET eol = BUFFER_LENGTH
          END
          READ_ASCII (last + 1) line (eol - last - 1)
        END
      END
      PATCH_IF (last >= 0) BEGIN
        SET at = pos + eol + 1
        PATCH_IF ((~%line%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^    Continue() *\(//.*\)?$~) = 0) BEGIN
          SET at = pos + last + 1
        END
        INSERT_BYTES at (STRING_LENGTH ~    %bgse_notice%%LNL%~)
        WRITE_ASCIIE at ~    %bgse_notice%%LNL%~
      END
    END
    SET stop = pos
    SET pos = RINDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%  RESPONSE #~ (pos - 1))
  END
END

// The block that ends SCS's preparation when the engine holds an opener (tools/hook_rule.py:
// opener_twin): bgse_block is the guarded opener, bgse_question its condition without the "!". The
// twin asks it the other way round and keeps of each response only the opener's variables and timers
// (SetGlobal, SetGlobalTimer, SetGlobalTimerRandom), not the round timer castspell, which the engine's
// first action sets; then Continue(), so the engine takes that round in the same pass.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_opener_twin
  STR_VAR bgse_block = ~~
          bgse_question = ~~
  RET bgse_twin
BEGIN
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE asked ~%bgse_block%~ BEGIN
    SET q = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~!%bgse_question%~)
    PATCH_IF (q >= 0) BEGIN
      DELETE_BYTES q 1
    END
  END
  SET then = INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~ ~%asked%~)
  INNER_PATCH ~%asked%~ BEGIN
    READ_ASCII 0 trig (then)
    READ_ASCII then resp (BUFFER_LENGTH - then)
  END
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE resp ~%resp%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    \([A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*\)(.*%LNL%~ BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT whole ~%MATCH0%~
      TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH1%~
      TEXT_SPRINT kept ~~
      PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%|~ ~|SetGlobal|SetGlobalTimer|SetGlobalTimerRandom|~) >= 0)
          AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    SetGlobalTimer\(Random\)?("castspell","LOCALS",~ ~%whole%~) < 0) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT kept ~%whole%~
      END
    END ~%kept%~
    // Continue() closes each response: before the block's END and before each RESPONSE line but the
    // first, from the last one up.
    SET first = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%  RESPONSE #~)
    SET pos = RINDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%END%LNL%~ BUFFER_LENGTH)
    INSERT_BYTES pos (STRING_LENGTH ~%LNL%    Continue()~)
    WRITE_ASCIIE pos ~%LNL%    Continue()~
    SET pos = RINDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%  RESPONSE #~ BUFFER_LENGTH)
    WHILE (pos > first) BEGIN
      INSERT_BYTES pos (STRING_LENGTH ~%LNL%    Continue()~)
      WRITE_ASCIIE pos ~%LNL%    Continue()~
      SET pos = RINDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%  RESPONSE #~ (pos - 1))
    END
  END
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_twin ~%trig%%resp%~
END

// Hook one decompiled SCS script; bgse_script is its resref in lower case, bgse_teleports the
// spells that move their caster, bgse_invisible those that make their target invisible,
// bgse_improved those of Improved Invisibility, bgse_innate those whose files say innate and
// bgse_vanish those that remove their target (|NAME| entries in upper case: resrefs, SPELL.IDS names
// and numbers); bgse_times the game's timer names (bgse_times_list). bgse_result is hooked, not-scs,
// unsafe-name, no-castspell, already-hooked or no-anchor; only "hooked" changes bgse_baf. bgse_clouds
// counts the cloud blocks that stand aside, bgse_hunts the hunting blocks, bgse_jumps the scripted
// jumps into the fight, bgse_hides the blocks that give the creature free invisibility, bgse_preps
// SCS's preparation blocks, bgse_exits its vanishing exits, bgse_idles its idle gates that ask the engine
// first; bgse_teleporter is 1 when a hooked script
// teleports its creature by script, bgse_hider when it makes its creature invisible for free, and
// bgse_gifts lists the real abilities that stand in for that (bgse_block_gifts), each once, in the
// order of its blocks.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_hook_baf
  STR_VAR bgse_baf = ~~
          bgse_script = ~~
          bgse_teleports = ~|~
          bgse_invisible = ~|~
          bgse_improved = ~|~
          bgse_innate = ~|~
          bgse_vanish = ~|~
          bgse_times = ~|~
  RET bgse_result bgse_family bgse_copies bgse_clouds bgse_hunts bgse_jumps bgse_hides bgse_preps bgse_exits bgse_idles
      bgse_teleporter bgse_hider bgse_gifts bgse_baf
BEGIN
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_result ~not-scs~
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_family ~~
  SET bgse_copies = 0
  SET bgse_clouds = 0
  SET bgse_hunts = 0
  SET bgse_jumps = 0
  SET bgse_hides = 0
  SET bgse_preps = 0
  SET bgse_exits = 0
  SET bgse_idles = 0
  SET bgse_teleporter = 0
  SET bgse_hider = 0
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_gifts ~|~
  TEXT_SPRINT gifts ~|~
  SET teleporting = 0
  // The checks look at the text in place: each look at a whole script through its variable copies it.
  INNER_PATCH_SAVE bgse_baf ~%bgse_baf%~ BEGIN
    PATCH_IF (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%MNL%~) >= 0) BEGIN
      REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%MNL%~ ~~
    END
    PATCH_IF (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~DMWW_mage_~) >= 0) BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_family ~mage~
    END ELSE PATCH_IF (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~DMWW_priest_~) >= 0) BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_family ~priest~
    END ELSE PATCH_IF (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~DMWW_genai_~) >= 0) BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_family ~fighter~
    END ELSE PATCH_IF (INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_INSENSITIVE ~DMWW_[a-z_]+_difficulty~) >= 0) BEGIN
      // Any other SCS difficulty setting (fiend, dragon, vampire, genie, ...): a monster script.
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_family ~monster~
    END
    SET castspell = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~GlobalTimerNotExpired("castspell","LOCALS")~)
    SET claimed = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~BGSE_Claim~)
  END
  PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_family%~ = 0) BEGIN
    TEXT_SPRINT bgse_result ~not-scs~
  END ELSE PATCH_IF (INDEX (EXACT_MATCH ~'~ ~%bgse_script%~) >= 0) OR (INDEX (EXACT_MATCH ~"~ ~%bgse_script%~) >= 0)
      OR (INDEX (EXACT_MATCH ~\~ ~%bgse_script%~) >= 0) BEGIN
    // The name goes into Lua text inside a BAF string.
    TEXT_SPRINT bgse_result ~unsafe-name~
  END ELSE PATCH_IF (castspell < 0) BEGIN
    TEXT_SPRINT bgse_result ~no-castspell~
  END ELSE PATCH_IF (claimed >= 0) BEGIN
    TEXT_SPRINT bgse_result ~already-hooked~
  END ELSE BEGIN
    // Block boundaries and flags. They go into records in strings, not into variables of their
    // own: each function call copies every variable, so the thousands of a big script would slow
    // down every call. A block's flags are the bits of one number: 1 book, 2 items, 4 special, 8 pick,
    // 16 lastseen, 32 encounter, 64 copy, 128 cloud, 256 hunt, 512 jump, 1024 and 2048 plain and
    // improved free invisibility, 4096 maybe SCS's preparation, 8192 vanishing exit, 16384 idle gate. plan has a record
    // for each block from the anchor on with flags (the others have none), its number, start, end and
    // flags as longs; edits and tail_edits one for each block above the anchor and from it that stands
    // aside or, above it, may be the preparation, its start, end and flags.
    SET n = 0
    SET anchor = 0 - 1
    SET at = 0
    TEXT_SPRINT plan ~~
    TEXT_SPRINT edits ~~
    TEXT_SPRINT tail_edits ~~
    SET hides_known = (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_invisible%~ > 1) ? 1 : 0
    SET teleports_known = (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_teleports%~ > 1) ? 1 : 0
    INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_baf%~ BEGIN
      SET pos = 0
      WHILE (pos >= 0) BEGIN
        SET stop = 0 - 1
        SET start = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^IF%LNL%~ pos)
        PATCH_IF (start >= 0) BEGIN
          SET end = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%END%LNL%~ start)
          PATCH_IF (end >= 0) BEGIN
            SET stop = end + 5
          END
        END
        PATCH_IF (stop < 0) BEGIN
          SET pos = 0 - 1
        END ELSE BEGIN
          SET flags = 0
          READ_ASCII start block (stop - start)
          PATCH_IF (hides_known = 1)
              AND (INDEX (CASE_INSENSITIVE ~^    \(\(ApplySpellRES\|ForceSpellRES\|ReallyForceSpellRES\|SpellNoDecRES\)("[^"]*",Myself)\|\(ApplySpell\|ForceSpell\|ReallyForceSpell\|SpellNoDec\)(Myself,\)~ ~%block%~) >= 0)
              AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~Myself~ ~%block%~) >= 0) BEGIN
            // SCS's free invisibility, above and below the anchor (every such cast names Myself, and
            // only a block with a cast or application at the creature itself can give it).
            LPF bgse_hide_block STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%block%~ bgse_invisible = EVAL ~%bgse_invisible%~
              bgse_improved = EVAL ~%bgse_improved%~ RET bgse_hide END
            SET flags = bgse_hide * 1024
            PATCH_IF (bgse_hide > 0) BEGIN
              // The real abilities that stand in for it, each once in the script.
              LPF bgse_block_gifts STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%block%~ bgse_invisible = EVAL ~%bgse_invisible%~
                  bgse_improved = EVAL ~%bgse_improved%~ bgse_innate = EVAL ~%bgse_innate%~ bgse_times = EVAL ~%bgse_times%~
                RET bgse_gifts END
              INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_gifts%~ BEGIN
                REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~\([RI]\):\([^|]+\)~ BEGIN
                  PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~:%MATCH2%|~ ~%gifts%~) < 0) BEGIN
                    TEXT_SPRINT gifts ~%gifts%%MATCH1%:%MATCH2%|~
                  END
                END ~%MATCH0%~
              END
            END
          END
          PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_INSENSITIVE ~chas\|teleportpursuetimer\|"detect"~ ~%block%~) >= 0)
              OR (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~OpenDoor(NearestDoor)\|!See(\|!Detect(~ ~%block%~) >= 0) BEGIN
            // SCS's hunt, above and below the anchor (only blocks with these words can be part
            // of it: a pursuit needs a trigger that says the creature does not see or detect
            // someone).
            LPF bgse_hunt_block STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%block%~ RET bgse_hunt END
            SET flags = flags BOR (bgse_hunt * 256)
          END
          PATCH_IF (teleports_known = 1) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~ForceSpell~ ~%block%~) >= 0) BEGIN
            // Its scripted teleports; a jump into the fight that is not part of the hunt.
            LPF bgse_block_teleports STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%block%~ bgse_teleports = EVAL ~%bgse_teleports%~
              RET bgse_scripted bgse_jump END
            PATCH_IF (bgse_scripted > 0) BEGIN
              SET teleporting = 1
            END
            PATCH_IF (bgse_jump = 1) AND ((flags BAND 256) = 0) BEGIN
              SET flags = flags BOR 512
            END
          END
          PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~^  \(HPPercentLT\|HPLT\)(Myself,~ ~%block%~) >= 0) BEGIN
            // SCS's vanishing exits, above and below the anchor (each checks the creature's own hit
            // points so).
            LPF bgse_exit_block STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%block%~ bgse_vanish = EVAL ~%bgse_vanish%~ RET bgse_exit END
            SET flags = flags BOR (bgse_exit * 8192)
          END
          PATCH_IF (anchor < 0) BEGIN
            // SCS's cloud escape or stand-still (tools/hook_rule.py: is_cloud); only those above
            // the anchor change.
            SET then = INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~ ~%block%~)
            PATCH_IF (then > 0) BEGIN
              INNER_PATCH ~%block%~ BEGIN
                READ_ASCII 0 trig (then)
                READ_ASCII then resp (BUFFER_LENGTH - then)
              END
              PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~SetGlobalTimer("seencloud","LOCALS",~ ~%resp%~) >= 0) BEGIN
                SET flags = flags BOR 128
              END ELSE PATCH_IF ((~%trig%~ STRING_CONTAINS_REGEXP ~%LNL% +Heard(\[ANYONE\],\(40[4-9]\|41[0-3]\))~) = 0) BEGIN
                // It hears a marker's shout (not !Heard). Every response is NoAction() alone, or
                // it runs from the marker it heard once a response with nothing else but
                // SetInterrupt.
                SET still_parts = 0
                SET still_actions = 0
                SET still_waits = 0
                SET still_runs = 0
                SET still_switches = 0
                INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
                  COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%  RESPONSE #~ still_parts
                  COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(~ still_actions
                  COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    NoAction()~ still_waits
                  COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    RunAwayFrom[A-Za-z]*(LastHeardBy(Myself),~ still_runs
                  COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    SetInterrupt(~ still_switches
                END
                PATCH_IF (still_parts > 0) AND (((still_actions = still_parts) AND (still_waits = still_parts))
                    OR ((still_runs = still_parts) AND (still_actions = still_runs + still_switches))) BEGIN
                  SET flags = flags BOR 128
                END
              END
              // SCS's idle gate (tools/hook_rule.py: is_idle): the creature perceives no enemy, is not in a
              // fight, and every response is NoAction() alone; only those above the anchor change.
              PATCH_IF ((~%trig%~ STRING_CONTAINS_REGEXP ~%LNL% +!Global("inafight","LOCALS",1)~) = 0)
                  AND ((~%trig%~ STRING_CONTAINS_REGEXP ~%LNL% +!\(See\|Detect\)(NearestEnemyOf(Myself))~) = 0) BEGIN
                SET idle_parts = 0
                SET idle_actions = 0
                SET idle_waits = 0
                INNER_PATCH ~%resp%~ BEGIN
                  COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%  RESPONSE #~ idle_parts
                  COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*(~ idle_actions
                  COUNT_REGEXP_INSTANCES CASE_SENSITIVE ~^    NoAction()~ idle_waits
                END
                PATCH_IF (idle_parts > 0) AND (idle_actions = idle_parts) AND (idle_waits = idle_parts) BEGIN
                  SET flags = flags BOR 16384
                END
              END
            END
          END
          PATCH_IF (anchor < 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~castspell~ ~%block%~) < 0) BEGIN
            // Cannot be the anchor and nothing before the anchor is copied.
          END ELSE PATCH_IF (anchor >= 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~Continue()\|ForceSpell\|SpellNoDec\|ApplySpell~ ~%block%~) < 0) BEGIN
            // Neither bookkeeping nor a target pick (no Continue) nor a special (no ForceSpell,
            // SpellNoDec or ApplySpell), but it may still do more than an ordinary combat round.
            SET then = INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%THEN%LNL%~ ~%block%~)
            PATCH_IF (then > 0) BEGIN
              INNER_PATCH ~%block%~ BEGIN
                READ_ASCII 0 trig (then)
                READ_ASCII then resp (BUFFER_LENGTH - then)
              END
              PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~Die()~ ~%trig%~) >= 0) BEGIN
                SET flags = flags BOR 32
              END ELSE BEGIN
                LPF bgse_foreign_actions STR_VAR bgse_resp = EVAL ~%resp%~ RET bgse_foreign END
                PATCH_IF (bgse_foreign > 0) BEGIN
                  SET flags = flags BOR 32
                END
              END
              // lastseen decides only for an encounter here, as in bgse_classify_block.
              PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 32) = 32) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~LastSeenBy(Myself)~ ~%block%~) >= 0) BEGIN
                SET flags = flags BOR 16
              END
            END
          END ELSE BEGIN
            LPF bgse_classify_block INT_VAR bgse_seek = (anchor < 0) ? 1 : 0 STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%block%~
              RET bgse_anchor bgse_flags END
            PATCH_IF (anchor < 0) AND (bgse_anchor = 1) BEGIN
              SET anchor = n
              SET at = start
            END
            PATCH_IF (anchor >= 0) BEGIN
              SET flags = flags BOR bgse_flags
            END
          END
          PATCH_IF (anchor < 0) BEGIN
            // Above the anchor: SCS's preparation can only be a block with these words.
            PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE ~ReallyForceSpell\|SetGlobal("instantprep","LOCALS",1)~ ~%block%~) >= 0) BEGIN
              SET flags = flags BOR 4096
            END
            PATCH_IF (flags > 0) BEGIN
              INNER_PATCH_SAVE edits ~%edits%~ BEGIN
                INSERT_BYTES BUFFER_LENGTH 12
                WRITE_LONG (BUFFER_LENGTH - 12) start
                WRITE_LONG (BUFFER_LENGTH - 8) stop
                WRITE_LONG (BUFFER_LENGTH - 4) flags
              END
            END
          END ELSE PATCH_IF (flags > 0) BEGIN
            INNER_PATCH_SAVE plan ~%plan%~ BEGIN
              INSERT_BYTES BUFFER_LENGTH 16
              WRITE_LONG (BUFFER_LENGTH - 16) n
              WRITE_LONG (BUFFER_LENGTH - 12) start
              WRITE_LONG (BUFFER_LENGTH - 8) stop
              WRITE_LONG (BUFFER_LENGTH - 4) flags
            END
            PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 12032) > 0) BEGIN
              INNER_PATCH_SAVE tail_edits ~%tail_edits%~ BEGIN
                INSERT_BYTES BUFFER_LENGTH 12
                WRITE_LONG (BUFFER_LENGTH - 12) start
                WRITE_LONG (BUFFER_LENGTH - 8) stop
                WRITE_LONG (BUFFER_LENGTH - 4) flags
              END
            END
          END
          SET n += 1
          SET pos = stop
        END
      END
    END
    TEXT_SPRINT bgse_gifts ~|~
    PATCH_IF (anchor < 0) BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_result ~no-anchor~
    END ELSE BEGIN
      // Bookkeeping runs that carry items or self-applied spells; the record after a block's is the
      // next block's only when its number follows.
      SET records = (STRING_LENGTH ~%plan%~) / 16
      INNER_PATCH_SAVE plan ~%plan%~ BEGIN
        SET i = 0
        WHILE (i < records) BEGIN
          READ_LONG (16 * i + 12) flags
          PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 1) = 1) BEGIN
            READ_LONG (16 * i) first
            SET j = i
            SET carries = 0
            WHILE ((flags BAND 1) = 1) BEGIN
              PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 2) = 2) BEGIN
                SET carries = 1
              END
              SET j += 1
              SET flags = 0
              PATCH_IF (j < records) BEGIN
                READ_LONG (16 * j) number
                PATCH_IF (number = first + j - i) BEGIN
                  READ_LONG (16 * j + 12) flags
                END
              END
            END
            PATCH_IF (carries = 1) BEGIN
              FOR (k = i; k < j; k += 1) BEGIN
                READ_LONG (16 * k + 12) flags
                PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 768) = 0) BEGIN
                  WRITE_LONG (16 * k + 12) (flags BOR 64)
                END
              END
            END
            SET i = j
          END ELSE BEGIN
            SET i += 1
          END
        END
        // Special abilities and blocks that do more than an ordinary combat round, with the
        // target picks right before them when they aim at LastSeenBy; never SCS's hunt or its
        // scripted jumps into the fight.
        FOR (i = 0; i < records; i += 1) BEGIN
          READ_LONG (16 * i + 12) flags
          PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 36) > 0) AND ((flags BAND 768) = 0) BEGIN
            WRITE_LONG (16 * i + 12) (flags BOR 64)
            PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 16) = 16) BEGIN
              READ_LONG (16 * i) number
              SET k = i - 1
              SET walking = 1
              WHILE (walking = 1) BEGIN
                SET picked = 0
                PATCH_IF (k >= 0) BEGIN
                  READ_LONG (16 * k) before
                  PATCH_IF (before = number - (i - k)) BEGIN
                    READ_LONG (16 * k + 12) picked
                  END
                END
                PATCH_IF ((picked BAND 8) = 8) BEGIN
                  WRITE_LONG (16 * k + 12) (picked BOR 64)
                  SET k -= 1
                END ELSE BEGIN
                  SET walking = 0
                END
              END
            END
          END
        END
      END
      // The copies go above the hook in their order.
      TEXT_SPRINT copied ~~
      INNER_PATCH ~%plan%~ BEGIN
        FOR (i = 0; i < records; i += 1) BEGIN
          READ_LONG (16 * i + 12) flags
          PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 64) = 64) BEGIN
            READ_ASCII (16 * i + 4) record (12)
            TEXT_SPRINT copied ~%copied%%record%~
          END
        END
      END
      TEXT_SPRINT guard ~EEex_LuaTrigger("return BGSE_Claim and BGSE_Claim(EEex_LuaTrigger_Object,'%bgse_family%','%bgse_script%') or false")~
      TEXT_SPRINT insert ~~
      SET count = (STRING_LENGTH ~%copied%~) / 12
      INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_baf%~ BEGIN
        FOR (k = 0; k < count; k += 1) BEGIN
          INNER_PATCH ~%copied%~ BEGIN
            READ_LONG (12 * k) s
            READ_LONG (12 * k + 4) e
            READ_LONG (12 * k + 8) flags
          END
          READ_ASCII s copy (e - s)
          // A copy that gives free invisibility or is a vanishing exit stands aside as its original does.
          TEXT_SPRINT extra ~~
          PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 3072) > 0) BEGIN
            TEXT_SPRINT kind ~plain~
            PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 2048) = 2048) BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT kind ~improved~
            END
            TEXT_SPRINT extra ~  !EEex_LuaTrigger("return BGSE_Hide and BGSE_Hide(EEex_LuaTrigger_Object,'%bgse_family%','%bgse_script%','%kind%') or false")~
          END
          PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 8192) = 8192) BEGIN
            PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%extra%~ > 0) BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT extra ~%extra%%LNL%~
            END
            TEXT_SPRINT extra ~%extra%  !EEex_LuaTrigger("return BGSE_Stay and BGSE_Stay(EEex_LuaTrigger_Object,'%bgse_family%','%bgse_script%') or false")~
          END
          PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%extra%~ > 0) BEGIN
            INNER_PATCH_SAVE copy ~%copy%~ BEGIN
              LPF bgse_aside INT_VAR bgse_from = 0 bgse_to = BUFFER_LENGTH STR_VAR bgse_lines = EVAL ~%extra%~ END
            END
          END
          INNER_PATCH ~%copy%~ BEGIN
            READ_ASCII 3 rest (BUFFER_LENGTH - 3)
          END
          TEXT_SPRINT insert ~%insert%IF%LNL%  %guard%%LNL%%rest%%LNL%~
          SET bgse_copies += 1
        END
      END
      // SCS's cloud blocks above the hook stand aside while the engine weighs danger zones for
      // the creature (tools/hook_rule.py: stand_aside), its hunting blocks and scripted jumps above
      // and below the hook while the engine drives it, and its free invisibility where the engine
      // hides the creature its own way. Each such block changes on its own, and the parts above and
      // below the hook are put together again in their order, in pieces of some 64 KB: a change in
      // a whole part would copy all of it each time.
      TEXT_SPRINT zone_line ~  !EEex_LuaTrigger("return BGSE_Zones and BGSE_Zones(EEex_LuaTrigger_Object,'%bgse_family%','%bgse_script%') or false")~
      TEXT_SPRINT search_line ~  !EEex_LuaTrigger("return BGSE_Search and BGSE_Search(EEex_LuaTrigger_Object,'%bgse_family%','%bgse_script%') or false")~
      TEXT_SPRINT plain_line ~  !EEex_LuaTrigger("return BGSE_Hide and BGSE_Hide(EEex_LuaTrigger_Object,'%bgse_family%','%bgse_script%','plain') or false")~
      TEXT_SPRINT improved_line ~  !EEex_LuaTrigger("return BGSE_Hide and BGSE_Hide(EEex_LuaTrigger_Object,'%bgse_family%','%bgse_script%','improved') or false")~
      TEXT_SPRINT stay_line ~  !EEex_LuaTrigger("return BGSE_Stay and BGSE_Stay(EEex_LuaTrigger_Object,'%bgse_family%','%bgse_script%') or false")~
      TEXT_SPRINT head ~~
      TEXT_SPRINT tail ~~
      INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_baf%~ BEGIN
        FOR (part = 0; part < 2; part += 1) BEGIN
          PATCH_IF (part = 0) BEGIN
            TEXT_SPRINT list ~%edits%~
            SET from = 0
            SET to = at
          END ELSE BEGIN
            TEXT_SPRINT list ~%tail_edits%~
            SET from = at
            SET to = BUFFER_LENGTH
          END
          TEXT_SPRINT whole ~~
          TEXT_SPRINT piece ~~
          SET size = 0
          SET count = (STRING_LENGTH ~%list%~) / 12
          FOR (k = 0; k < count; k += 1) BEGIN
            INNER_PATCH ~%list%~ BEGIN
              READ_LONG (12 * k) s
              READ_LONG (12 * k + 4) e
              READ_LONG (12 * k + 8) flags
            END
            // Only those above the anchor yield to the zones (the anchor's own cloud flag goes unused).
            TEXT_SPRINT lines ~~
            PATCH_IF (part = 0) AND ((flags BAND 128) = 128) BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT lines ~%zone_line%~
              SET bgse_clouds += 1
            END
            PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 768) > 0) BEGIN
              PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%lines%~ > 0) BEGIN
                TEXT_SPRINT lines ~%lines%%LNL%~
              END
              TEXT_SPRINT lines ~%lines%%search_line%~
              PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 256) = 256) BEGIN
                SET bgse_hunts += 1
              END ELSE BEGIN
                SET bgse_jumps += 1
              END
            END
            PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 3072) > 0) BEGIN
              PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%lines%~ > 0) BEGIN
                TEXT_SPRINT lines ~%lines%%LNL%~
              END
              PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 2048) = 2048) BEGIN
                TEXT_SPRINT lines ~%lines%%improved_line%~
              END ELSE BEGIN
                TEXT_SPRINT lines ~%lines%%plain_line%~
              END
              SET bgse_hides += 1
            END
            READ_ASCII s block (e - s)
            // SCS's preparation asks the engine.
            TEXT_SPRINT bgse_prep ~~
            PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 4096) = 4096) BEGIN
              LPF bgse_prep_block STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%block%~ RET bgse_prep bgse_cast bgse_spent END
            END
            PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_prep%~ > 0) BEGIN
              PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%lines%~ > 0) BEGIN
                TEXT_SPRINT lines ~%lines%%LNL%~
              END
              TEXT_SPRINT lines ~%lines%  !EEex_LuaTrigger("return BGSE_Prep and BGSE_Prep(EEex_LuaTrigger_Object,'%bgse_family%','%bgse_script%','%bgse_prep%','%bgse_cast%','%bgse_spent%') or false")~
              SET bgse_preps += 1
            END
            // A vanishing exit stays out while the engine keeps the creature in the fight.
            PATCH_IF ((flags BAND 8192) = 8192) BEGIN
              PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%lines%~ > 0) BEGIN
                TEXT_SPRINT lines ~%lines%%LNL%~
              END
              TEXT_SPRINT lines ~%lines%%stay_line%~
              SET bgse_exits += 1
            END
            // SCS's idle gate holds only when the engine has no decision: the hook's own question.
            PATCH_IF (part = 0) AND ((flags BAND 16384) = 16384) BEGIN
              PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%lines%~ > 0) BEGIN
                TEXT_SPRINT lines ~%lines%%LNL%~
              END
              TEXT_SPRINT lines ~%lines%  !%guard%~
              SET bgse_idles += 1
            END
            INNER_PATCH_SAVE block ~%block%~ BEGIN
              PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%lines%~ > 0) BEGIN
                LPF bgse_aside INT_VAR bgse_from = 0 bgse_to = BUFFER_LENGTH STR_VAR bgse_lines = EVAL ~%lines%~ END
              END
              // The engine hears of the preparation that ran; it chooses the first round itself, and an
              // opener it holds still ends SCS's preparation (bgse_opener_twin, right after the opener).
              PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_prep%~ > 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%bgse_prep%|~ ~|opener|~) < 0) BEGIN
                LPF bgse_notify INT_VAR bgse_from = 0
                  STR_VAR bgse_notice = EVAL ~EEex_LuaAction("if BGSE_Prepped then BGSE_Prepped(EEex_LuaAction_Object,'%bgse_family%','%bgse_script%','%bgse_prep%','%bgse_cast%','%bgse_spent%') end")~ END
              END ELSE PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_prep%~ > 0) BEGIN
                SET close = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%LNL%END%LNL%~) + STRING_LENGTH ~%LNL%END%LNL%~
                READ_ASCII 0 guarded (close)
                LPF bgse_opener_twin STR_VAR bgse_block = EVAL ~%guarded%~
                  bgse_question = EVAL ~EEex_LuaTrigger("return BGSE_Prep and BGSE_Prep(EEex_LuaTrigger_Object,'%bgse_family%','%bgse_script%','%bgse_prep%','%bgse_cast%','%bgse_spent%') or false")~
                  RET bgse_twin END
                INSERT_BYTES close (STRING_LENGTH ~%LNL%%bgse_twin%~)
                WRITE_ASCIIE close ~%LNL%%bgse_twin%~
              END
            END
            TEXT_SPRINT gap ~~
            PATCH_IF (s > from) BEGIN
              READ_ASCII from gap (s - from)
            END
            TEXT_SPRINT piece ~%piece%%gap%%block%~
            SET size += (s - from) + STRING_LENGTH ~%block%~
            PATCH_IF (size > 65536) BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT whole ~%whole%%piece%~
              TEXT_SPRINT piece ~~
              SET size = 0
            END
            SET from = e
          END
          TEXT_SPRINT gap ~~
          PATCH_IF (to > from) BEGIN
            READ_ASCII from gap (to - from)
          END
          PATCH_IF (part = 0) BEGIN
            TEXT_SPRINT head ~%whole%%piece%%gap%~
          END ELSE BEGIN
            TEXT_SPRINT tail ~%whole%%piece%%gap%~
          END
        END
      END
      SET bgse_teleporter = teleporting
      SET bgse_hider = (bgse_hides > 0) ? 1 : 0
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_gifts ~%gifts%~
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_baf ~%head%%insert%IF%LNL%  %guard%%LNL%THEN%LNL%  RESPONSE #100%LNL%    EEex_LuaAction("if BGSE_Act then BGSE_Act(EEex_LuaAction_Object) end")%LNL%END%LNL%%LNL%%tail%~
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_result ~hooked~
    END
  END
END

// Hook the BCS in the patch buffer; bgse_script is its resref in lower case. A script that
// fails to decompile, patch or compile is left exactly as it was (bgse_result "failed").
// bgse_teleports and bgse_checked (|NAME| entries in upper case) are the spells known to move
// their caster and all spells looked up so far for that: the spells of the script's casts without a
// spellbook are looked up in the game once each (bgse_moves_caster), and both come back with them.
// bgse_invisible, bgse_improved, bgse_innate, bgse_vanish and bgse_looked do the same for the spells
// known to make their target invisible, those of Improved Invisibility, those whose files say innate,
// those that remove their target and all spells looked up for that, from the script's casts and
// applications at the creature itself (bgse_look_spell). bgse_times are the game's timer names
// (bgse_times_list); bgse_gifts as in bgse_hook_baf.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_hook_bcs
  STR_VAR bgse_script = ~~
          bgse_teleports = ~|~
          bgse_checked = ~|~
          bgse_invisible = ~|~
          bgse_improved = ~|~
          bgse_innate = ~|~
          bgse_vanish = ~|~
          bgse_looked = ~|~
          bgse_times = ~|~
  RET bgse_result bgse_family bgse_copies bgse_clouds bgse_hunts bgse_jumps bgse_hides bgse_preps bgse_exits bgse_idles
      bgse_teleporter bgse_hider bgse_gifts bgse_teleports bgse_checked bgse_invisible bgse_improved bgse_innate bgse_vanish
      bgse_looked
BEGIN
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_result ~failed~
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_family ~~
  SET bgse_copies = 0
  SET bgse_clouds = 0
  SET bgse_hunts = 0
  SET bgse_jumps = 0
  SET bgse_hides = 0
  SET bgse_preps = 0
  SET bgse_exits = 0
  SET bgse_idles = 0
  SET bgse_teleporter = 0
  SET bgse_hider = 0
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_gifts ~|~
  READ_ASCII 0 bcs (BUFFER_LENGTH)
  PATCH_TRY
    INNER_PATCH_SAVE baf ~%bcs%~ BEGIN
      DECOMPILE_BCS_TO_BAF
    END
    // The spells of its casts and applications, from the script without its comments.
    INNER_PATCH_SAVE text ~%baf%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_TEXTUALLY CASE_SENSITIVE ~ *//.*$~ ~~
    END
    LPF bgse_cast_spells STR_VAR bgse_text = EVAL ~%text%~ RET bgse_spells END
    INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_spells%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~\([RI]\)=\([^|]+\)~ BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT form ~%MATCH1%~
        TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH2%~
        PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%|~ ~%bgse_checked%~) < 0) BEGIN
          LPF bgse_moves_caster STR_VAR bgse_form = EVAL ~%form%~ bgse_spell = EVAL ~%name%~ RET bgse_moves END
          TEXT_SPRINT bgse_checked ~%bgse_checked%%name%|~
          PATCH_IF (bgse_moves = 1) BEGIN
            TEXT_SPRINT bgse_teleports ~%bgse_teleports%%name%|~
          END
        END
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
    LPF bgse_self_spells STR_VAR bgse_text = EVAL ~%text%~ RET bgse_spells END
    INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_spells%~ BEGIN
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~\([RI]\)=\([^|]+\)~ BEGIN
        LPF bgse_look_spell STR_VAR bgse_form = EVAL ~%MATCH1%~ bgse_spell = EVAL ~%MATCH2%~ bgse_looked = EVAL ~%bgse_looked%~
            bgse_invisible = EVAL ~%bgse_invisible%~ bgse_improved = EVAL ~%bgse_improved%~ bgse_innate = EVAL ~%bgse_innate%~
            bgse_vanish = EVAL ~%bgse_vanish%~
          RET bgse_looked bgse_invisible bgse_improved bgse_innate bgse_vanish END
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    END
    LPF bgse_hook_baf STR_VAR bgse_baf = EVAL ~%baf%~ bgse_script = EVAL ~%bgse_script%~ bgse_teleports = EVAL ~%bgse_teleports%~
        bgse_invisible = EVAL ~%bgse_invisible%~ bgse_improved = EVAL ~%bgse_improved%~ bgse_innate = EVAL ~%bgse_innate%~
        bgse_vanish = EVAL ~%bgse_vanish%~ bgse_times = EVAL ~%bgse_times%~
      RET bgse_result bgse_family bgse_copies bgse_clouds bgse_hunts bgse_jumps bgse_hides bgse_preps bgse_exits bgse_idles
          bgse_teleporter bgse_hider bgse_gifts bgse_baf END
    PATCH_IF (~%bgse_result%~ STRING_EQUAL_CASE ~hooked~) BEGIN
      DELETE_BYTES 0 BUFFER_LENGTH
      INSERT_BYTES 0 (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_baf%~)
      WRITE_ASCIIE 0 ~%bgse_baf%~
      COMPILE_BAF_TO_BCS
    END
  WITH DEFAULT
    TEXT_SPRINT bgse_result ~failed~
    SET bgse_copies = 0
    SET bgse_clouds = 0
    SET bgse_hunts = 0
    SET bgse_jumps = 0
    SET bgse_hides = 0
    SET bgse_preps = 0
    SET bgse_exits = 0
    SET bgse_idles = 0
    SET bgse_teleporter = 0
    SET bgse_hider = 0
    TEXT_SPRINT bgse_gifts ~|~
    DELETE_BYTES 0 BUFFER_LENGTH
    INSERT_BYTES 0 (STRING_LENGTH ~%bcs%~)
    WRITE_ASCIIE 0 ~%bcs%~
  END
END

// Give the creature in the patch buffer (a CRE V1.0) the innate teleport BGSETELE when one of its
// scripts is a hooked script that teleports by script (bgse_teleporters, |script| entries in lower
// case) and none of its memorized spells moves its caster (tools/hook_rule.py: grants); its
// memorized spells are looked up once each, as in bgse_hook_bcs. bgse_grant is 1 when it got it. A
// creature file WeiDU cannot add the spell to is left exactly as it was.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_grant_teleport
  STR_VAR bgse_teleporters = ~|~
          bgse_teleports = ~|~
          bgse_checked = ~|~
  RET bgse_grant bgse_teleports bgse_checked
BEGIN
  SET bgse_grant = 0
  PATCH_IF (BUFFER_LENGTH >= 0x2d4) BEGIN
    READ_ASCII 0 signature (8)
    SET scripted = 0
    PATCH_IF (~%signature%~ STRING_EQUAL ~CRE V1.0~) BEGIN
      FOR (o = 0x248; o < 0x270; o += 8) BEGIN
        READ_ASCII o script (8) NULL
        TO_LOWER script
        PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%script%~ > 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%script%|~ ~%bgse_teleporters%~) >= 0) BEGIN
          SET scripted = 1
        END
      END
    END
    PATCH_IF (scripted = 1) BEGIN
      READ_LONG 0x2b0 at
      READ_LONG 0x2b4 count
      SET own = 0
      FOR (i = 0; (i < count) AND (own = 0); i += 1) BEGIN
        PATCH_IF (at + 12 * i + 8 <= BUFFER_LENGTH) BEGIN
          READ_ASCII (at + 12 * i) spell (8) NULL
          TO_UPPER spell
          PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%spell%~ > 0) BEGIN
            PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%spell%|~ ~%bgse_checked%~) < 0) BEGIN
              LPF bgse_moves_caster STR_VAR bgse_form = ~R~ bgse_spell = EVAL ~%spell%~ RET bgse_moves END
              TEXT_SPRINT bgse_checked ~%bgse_checked%%spell%|~
              PATCH_IF (bgse_moves = 1) BEGIN
                TEXT_SPRINT bgse_teleports ~%bgse_teleports%%spell%|~
              END
            END
            PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%spell%|~ ~%bgse_teleports%~) >= 0) BEGIN
              SET own = 1
            END
          END
        END
      END
      PATCH_IF (own = 0) BEGIN
        READ_ASCII 0 cre (BUFFER_LENGTH)
        PATCH_TRY
          ADD_KNOWN_SPELL ~BGSETELE~ #0 ~innate~
          ADD_MEMORIZED_SPELL ~BGSETELE~ #0 ~innate~ (1)
          SET bgse_grant = 1
        WITH DEFAULT
          SET bgse_grant = 0
          DELETE_BYTES 0 BUFFER_LENGTH
          INSERT_BYTES 0 (STRING_LENGTH ~%cre%~)
          WRITE_ASCIIE 0 ~%cre%~
        END
      END
    END
  END
END

// The game's tables for thieves' hide skills, read once: bgse_points has |ROW=START,LEVEL| entries
// for the rows of THIEFSKL.2DA (class and kit names: the skill points a player thief gets at the first
// level and at each level after it), bgse_kits |KITIDS=ROWNAME| entries for the rows of KITLIST.2DA
// (KIT.IDS values in decimal, the first row of each) and bgse_party |NAME| entries for the rows of
// PDIALOG.2DA (the joinable NPCs' script names), all in upper case. Columns are found by their
// names; a table the game lacks gives an empty list.
DEFINE_ACTION_FUNCTION bgse_skill_tables
  RET bgse_points bgse_kits bgse_party
BEGIN
  OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT bgse_points ~|~
  OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT bgse_kits ~|~
  OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT bgse_party ~|~
  ACTION_IF (FILE_EXISTS_IN_GAME ~thiefskl.2da~) BEGIN
    COPY_EXISTING ~thiefskl.2da~ ~override~
      LPF bgse_2da_pairs STR_VAR bgse_key = ~~ bgse_first = ~START_POINTS~ bgse_second = ~LEVEL_POINTS~ RET bgse_pairs END
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_points ~%bgse_pairs%~
    BUT_ONLY_IF_IT_CHANGES
  END
  ACTION_IF (FILE_EXISTS_IN_GAME ~kitlist.2da~) BEGIN
    COPY_EXISTING ~kitlist.2da~ ~override~
      LPF bgse_2da_pairs STR_VAR bgse_key = ~KITIDS~ bgse_first = ~ROWNAME~ bgse_second = ~~ RET bgse_pairs END
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_kits ~%bgse_pairs%~
    BUT_ONLY_IF_IT_CHANGES
  END
  ACTION_IF (FILE_EXISTS_IN_GAME ~pdialog.2da~) BEGIN
    COPY_EXISTING ~pdialog.2da~ ~override~
      LPF bgse_2da_pairs STR_VAR bgse_key = ~~ bgse_first = ~~ bgse_second = ~~ RET bgse_pairs END
      TEXT_SPRINT bgse_party ~%bgse_pairs%~
    BUT_ONLY_IF_IT_CHANGES
  END
END

// Entries of the 2DA in the patch buffer, one a data row, in upper case: |KEY=FIRST,SECOND|, where KEY
// is the column named bgse_key (the row's name when bgse_key is empty; a number such as 0x4021 in
// decimal), FIRST and SECOND those named bgse_first and bgse_second (left out when empty, with their
// separator). A row that lacks one of them is left out. The first line is the signature, the second
// the default value, the third names the columns after the rows' names.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_2da_pairs
  STR_VAR bgse_key = ~~
          bgse_first = ~~
          bgse_second = ~~
  RET bgse_pairs
BEGIN
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_pairs ~|~
  SET line = 0
  SET key_col = (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_key%~ = 0) ? 0 : (0 - 1)
  SET first_col = 0 - 1
  SET second_col = 0 - 1
  READ_ASCII 0 table (BUFFER_LENGTH)
  INNER_PATCH ~%table%~ BEGIN
    REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^[^%LNL%%MNL%]*[^ %TAB%%LNL%%MNL%][^%LNL%%MNL%]*~ BEGIN
      TEXT_SPRINT text ~%MATCH0%~
      SET col = 0
      TEXT_SPRINT key ~~
      TEXT_SPRINT first ~~
      TEXT_SPRINT second ~~
      INNER_PATCH ~%text%~ BEGIN
        REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~[^ %TAB%]+~ BEGIN
          PATCH_IF (line = 2) BEGIN
            // A column's data is one to the right of its name.
            PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_key%~ > 0) AND (~%MATCH0%~ STRING_EQUAL_CASE ~%bgse_key%~) BEGIN
              SET key_col = col + 1
            END
            PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_first%~ > 0) AND (~%MATCH0%~ STRING_EQUAL_CASE ~%bgse_first%~) BEGIN
              SET first_col = col + 1
            END
            PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_second%~ > 0) AND (~%MATCH0%~ STRING_EQUAL_CASE ~%bgse_second%~) BEGIN
              SET second_col = col + 1
            END
          END ELSE PATCH_IF (line > 2) BEGIN
            PATCH_IF (col = key_col) BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT key ~%MATCH0%~
            END
            PATCH_IF (col = first_col) BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT first ~%MATCH0%~
            END
            PATCH_IF (col = second_col) BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT second ~%MATCH0%~
            END
          END
          SET col += 1
        END ~%MATCH0%~
      END
      PATCH_IF (line > 2) AND (STRING_LENGTH ~%key%~ > 0)
          AND ((STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_first%~ = 0) OR (STRING_LENGTH ~%first%~ > 0))
          AND ((STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_second%~ = 0) OR (STRING_LENGTH ~%second%~ > 0)) BEGIN
        PATCH_IF ((~%key%~ STRING_MATCHES_REGEXP ~^0x[0-9a-fA-F]+$~) = 0) BEGIN
          SET number = key
          TEXT_SPRINT key ~%number%~
        END
        TEXT_SPRINT entry ~%key%~
        PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_first%~ > 0) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT entry ~%entry%=%first%~
        END
        PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_second%~ > 0) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT entry ~%entry%,%second%~
        END
        TO_UPPER entry
        PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%key%=~ ~%bgse_pairs%~) < 0)
            AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%entry%|~ ~%bgse_pairs%~) < 0) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT bgse_pairs ~%bgse_pairs%%entry%|~
        END
      END
      SET line += 1
    END ~%MATCH0%~
  END
END

// Give the thief in the patch buffer (a CRE V1.0) hide skills that fit its level when one of its
// scripts is a hooked script that makes its creature invisible for free (bgse_hiders, |script|
// entries in lower case; Christopher, 2026-10-26: thieves hide with their own Hide in Shadows, and
// their skill fits it; 2026-10-27: as high as a rogue could legally have it). Hide in Shadows and
// Move Silently each get half of the skill points a player thief of its kit (else its class) has at
// its thief level, all it could put into the two (bgse_points from THIEFSKL.2DA: the first level's
// points and those of each level after it; bgse_kits maps KIT.IDS values to kit names), never less
// than it has. Joinable NPCs (bgse_party) keep their skills. bgse_raised is 1 when a skill went up.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_raise_skills
  STR_VAR bgse_hiders = ~|~
          bgse_points = ~|~
          bgse_kits = ~|~
          bgse_party = ~|~
  RET bgse_raised
BEGIN
  SET bgse_raised = 0
  PATCH_IF (BUFFER_LENGTH >= 0x2d4) BEGIN
    READ_ASCII 0 signature (8)
    SET hider = 0
    PATCH_IF (~%signature%~ STRING_EQUAL ~CRE V1.0~) BEGIN
      FOR (o = 0x248; o < 0x270; o += 8) BEGIN
        READ_ASCII o script (8) NULL
        TO_LOWER script
        PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%script%~ > 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%script%|~ ~%bgse_hiders%~) >= 0) BEGIN
          SET hider = 1
        END
      END
    END
    PATCH_IF (hider = 1) BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0x280 name (32) NULL
      TO_UPPER name
      // Its thief level: multiclass levels go in the order of the class's name.
      READ_BYTE 0x273 class
      SET at = 0
      TEXT_SPRINT row ~~
      PATCH_IF (class = 4) BEGIN
        SET at = 0x234
        TEXT_SPRINT row ~THIEF~
      END ELSE PATCH_IF (class = 9) BEGIN
        SET at = 0x235
        TEXT_SPRINT row ~FIGHTER_THIEF~
      END ELSE PATCH_IF (class = 10) BEGIN
        SET at = 0x236
        TEXT_SPRINT row ~FIGHTER_MAGE_THIEF~
      END ELSE PATCH_IF (class = 13) BEGIN
        SET at = 0x235
        TEXT_SPRINT row ~MAGE_THIEF~
      END ELSE PATCH_IF (class = 15) BEGIN
        SET at = 0x235
        TEXT_SPRINT row ~CLERIC_THIEF~
      END
      PATCH_IF (at > 0) AND ((STRING_LENGTH ~%name%~ = 0) OR (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%|~ ~%bgse_party%~) < 0)) BEGIN
        // A kit (the high word, as KIT.IDS numbers it) that has a row of its own.
        READ_SHORT 0x246 kit
        PATCH_IF (kit > 0x4000) BEGIN
          SET p = INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%kit%=~ ~%bgse_kits%~)
          PATCH_IF (p >= 0) BEGIN
            SET from = p + STRING_LENGTH ~|%kit%=~
            INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_kits%~ BEGIN
              SET to = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|~ from)
              READ_ASCII from kit_row (to - from)
            END
            PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%kit_row%=~ ~%bgse_points%~) >= 0) BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT row ~%kit_row%~
            END
          END
        END
        PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%row%=~ ~%bgse_points%~) < 0) BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT row ~THIEF~
        END
        SET p = INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%row%=~ ~%bgse_points%~)
        PATCH_IF (p >= 0) BEGIN
          SET from = p + STRING_LENGTH ~|%row%=~
          INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_points%~ BEGIN
            SET comma = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~,~ from)
            SET to = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|~ from)
            READ_ASCII from start_points (comma - from)
            READ_ASCII (comma + 1) level_points (to - comma - 1)
          END
          PATCH_IF (IS_AN_INT start_points) AND (IS_AN_INT level_points) BEGIN
            READ_BYTE at level
            SET level = (level < 1) ? 1 : level
            SET target = (start_points + level_points * (level - 1)) / 2
            SET target = (target > 255) ? 255 : target
            FOR (s = 0; s < 2; s += 1) BEGIN
              SET skill = (s = 0) ? 0x45 : 0x68
              READ_BYTE skill value
              PATCH_IF (value < target) BEGIN
                WRITE_BYTE skill target
                SET bgse_raised = 1
              END
            END
          END
        END
      END
    END
  END
END

// The game's timer names (GTIMES.IDS), read once, as |NAME=SECONDS| entries in upper case: each line
// of two words whose first is a number (tools/hook_rule.py: read_times). Empty when the game lacks the
// file.
DEFINE_ACTION_FUNCTION bgse_times_list
  RET bgse_times
BEGIN
  OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT bgse_times ~|~
  ACTION_IF (FILE_EXISTS_IN_GAME ~gtimes.ids~) BEGIN
    COPY_EXISTING ~gtimes.ids~ ~override~
      REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^[ %TAB%]*\([0-9]+\)[ %TAB%]+\([^ %TAB%%LNL%%MNL%]+\)[ %TAB%%MNL%]*$~ BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH2%~
        TO_UPPER name
        TEXT_SPRINT bgse_times ~%bgse_times%%name%=%MATCH1%|~
      END ~%MATCH0%~
    BUT_ONLY_IF_IT_CHANGES
  END
END

// Give the creature in the patch buffer (a CRE V1.0) the real abilities that stand in for SCS's free
// invisibility (tools/hook_rule.py: creature_gifts, grant_resref): the gifts of its scripts
// (bgse_gifts_of, |script>FORM:SPELL:KIND:CHARGES:RECHARGE| entries, scripts in lower case and gifts as
// bgse_hook_baf lists them), each once in the order of its script slots, but no plain invisibility for
// a thief (it has thief levels: it hides by its skill), no invisibility of a kind it has a memorized
// innate ability of its own for, and nothing for a joinable NPC (bgse_party, as bgse_skill_tables reads
// it). A gift is the spell itself when it is an innate ability whose uses SCS counts, else its innate
// copy (bgse_gift_name). The creature knows it and has it memorized as an innate ability as often as SCS
// gives it (once when it comes back by itself; the most of two gifts of the same name). Each copy goes
// into bgse_copies (|NAME>RESREF:RECHARGE| entries) for bgse_create_gifts. A gift whose spell the game
// lacks is left out, and so is one whose copy name another spell of ours already has. Each copy name is ours
// and overwrites a resource under it. Spells are looked up once each (bgse_look_spell). bgse_given lists what
// the creature got, for the log. A creature file WeiDU cannot add the spells to is left exactly as it was.
DEFINE_PATCH_FUNCTION bgse_grant_gifts
  STR_VAR bgse_gifts_of = ~|~
          bgse_party = ~|~
          bgse_looked = ~|~
          bgse_invisible = ~|~
          bgse_improved = ~|~
          bgse_innate = ~|~
          bgse_copies = ~|~
  RET bgse_given bgse_looked bgse_invisible bgse_improved bgse_innate bgse_copies
BEGIN
  TEXT_SPRINT bgse_given ~~
  TEXT_SPRINT gifts ~|~
  PATCH_IF (BUFFER_LENGTH >= 0x2d4) BEGIN
    READ_ASCII 0 signature (8)
    PATCH_IF (~%signature%~ STRING_EQUAL ~CRE V1.0~) BEGIN
      // Its scripts' gifts; the same gift written another way counts once.
      FOR (o = 0x248; o < 0x270; o += 8) BEGIN
        READ_ASCII o script (8) NULL
        TO_LOWER script
        PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%script%~ > 0) BEGIN
          INNER_PATCH ~%bgse_gifts_of%~ BEGIN
            SET p = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%script%>~)
            WHILE (p >= 0) BEGIN
              SET from = p + STRING_LENGTH ~|%script%>~
              SET to = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|~ from)
              READ_ASCII from gift (to - from)
              READ_ASCII (from + 1) key (to - from - 1)
              PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~%key%|~ ~%gifts%~) < 0) BEGIN
                TEXT_SPRINT gifts ~%gifts%%gift%|~
              END
              SET p = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%script%>~ to)
            END
          END
        END
      END
    END
    PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%gifts%~ > 1) BEGIN
      READ_ASCII 0x280 name (32) NULL
      TO_UPPER name
      PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%name%~ > 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%name%|~ ~%bgse_party%~) >= 0) BEGIN
        TEXT_SPRINT gifts ~|~
      END
    END
    PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%gifts%~ > 1) BEGIN
      // Thief levels, and the kinds of its memorized innate invisibilities.
      READ_BYTE 0x273 class
      SET thief = ((class = 4) OR (class = 9) OR (class = 10) OR (class = 13) OR (class = 15)) ? 1 : 0
      SET own_plain = 0
      SET own_improved = 0
      READ_LONG 0x2b0 at
      READ_LONG 0x2b4 count
      FOR (i = 0; i < count; i += 1) BEGIN
        PATCH_IF (at + 12 * i + 8 <= BUFFER_LENGTH) BEGIN
          READ_ASCII (at + 12 * i) spell (8) NULL
          TO_UPPER spell
          PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%spell%~ > 0) BEGIN
            LPF bgse_look_spell STR_VAR bgse_form = ~R~ bgse_spell = EVAL ~%spell%~ bgse_looked = EVAL ~%bgse_looked%~
                bgse_invisible = EVAL ~%bgse_invisible%~ bgse_improved = EVAL ~%bgse_improved%~ bgse_innate = EVAL ~%bgse_innate%~
              RET bgse_looked bgse_invisible bgse_improved bgse_innate END
            PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%spell%|~ ~%bgse_innate%~) >= 0) BEGIN
              PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%spell%|~ ~%bgse_improved%~) >= 0) BEGIN
                SET own_improved = 1
              END ELSE PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%spell%|~ ~%bgse_invisible%~) >= 0) BEGIN
                SET own_plain = 1
              END
            END
          END
        END
      END
      // What each gift gives (grants, |NAME| entries, with how often in bgse_times_of) and the copies
      // that makes (made, NAME>RESREF:RECHARGE| entries).
      TEXT_SPRINT grants ~|~
      TEXT_SPRINT made ~~
      SET pos = 1
      WHILE (pos < STRING_LENGTH ~%gifts%~) BEGIN
        INNER_PATCH ~%gifts%~ BEGIN
          SET to = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|~ pos)
          READ_ASCII pos gift (to - pos)
        END
        SET pos = to + 1
        TEXT_SPRINT form ~~
        INNER_PATCH ~%gift%~ BEGIN
          REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^\([RI]\):\([^:]+\):\([^:]+\):\([^:]+\):\([^:]+\)$~ BEGIN
            TEXT_SPRINT form ~%MATCH1%~
            TEXT_SPRINT spell ~%MATCH2%~
            TEXT_SPRINT kind ~%MATCH3%~
            TEXT_SPRINT charges ~%MATCH4%~
            TEXT_SPRINT recharge ~%MATCH5%~
          END ~%MATCH0%~
        END
        SET keep = (STRING_LENGTH ~%form%~ > 0) ? 1 : 0
        PATCH_IF (keep = 1) AND (~%kind%~ STRING_EQUAL ~plain~) AND ((thief = 1) OR (own_plain = 1)) BEGIN
          SET keep = 0
        END
        PATCH_IF (keep = 1) AND (~%kind%~ STRING_EQUAL ~improved~) AND (own_improved = 1) BEGIN
          SET keep = 0
        END
        PATCH_IF (keep = 1) BEGIN
          LPF bgse_spell_res STR_VAR bgse_form = EVAL ~%form%~ bgse_spell = EVAL ~%spell%~ RET bgse_res END
          TEXT_SPRINT res ~%bgse_res%~
          TO_UPPER res
          SET keep = 0
          PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%res%~ > 0) AND (STRING_LENGTH ~%res%~ <= 8) BEGIN
            PATCH_IF (FILE_EXISTS_IN_GAME ~%res%.spl~) BEGIN
              SET keep = 1
            END
          END
        END
        PATCH_IF (keep = 1) BEGIN
          LPF bgse_look_spell STR_VAR bgse_form = ~R~ bgse_spell = EVAL ~%res%~ bgse_looked = EVAL ~%bgse_looked%~
              bgse_invisible = EVAL ~%bgse_invisible%~ bgse_improved = EVAL ~%bgse_improved%~ bgse_innate = EVAL ~%bgse_innate%~
            RET bgse_looked bgse_invisible bgse_improved bgse_innate END
          SET seconds = 0
          PATCH_IF (IS_AN_INT recharge) BEGIN
            SET seconds = recharge
          END
          SET times = 1
          PATCH_IF (IS_AN_INT charges) BEGIN
            SET times = charges
          END
          PATCH_IF (seconds = 0) AND (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%res%|~ ~%bgse_innate%~) >= 0) BEGIN
            TEXT_SPRINT grant ~%res%~
          END ELSE BEGIN
            LPF bgse_gift_name INT_VAR bgse_recharge = seconds STR_VAR bgse_res = EVAL ~%res%~ RET bgse_name END
            TEXT_SPRINT grant ~%bgse_name%~
            TEXT_SPRINT listed ~%bgse_copies%%made%~
            PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%grant%>~ ~%listed%~) >= 0) BEGIN
              PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%grant%>%res%:~ ~%listed%~) < 0) BEGIN
                SET keep = 0
              END
            END ELSE BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT made ~%made%%grant%>%res%:%seconds%|~
            END
          END
        END
        PATCH_IF (keep = 1) BEGIN
          PATCH_IF (INDEX (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|%grant%|~ ~%grants%~) < 0) BEGIN
            TEXT_SPRINT grants ~%grants%%grant%|~
            SET $bgse_times_of(~%grant%~) = times
          END ELSE PATCH_IF (times > $bgse_times_of(~%grant%~)) BEGIN
            SET $bgse_times_of(~%grant%~) = times
          END
        END
      END
      PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%grants%~ > 1) BEGIN
        READ_ASCII 0 cre (BUFFER_LENGTH)
        PATCH_TRY
          SET pos = 1
          WHILE (pos < STRING_LENGTH ~%grants%~) BEGIN
            INNER_PATCH ~%grants%~ BEGIN
              SET to = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|~ pos)
              READ_ASCII pos grant (to - pos)
            END
            SET pos = to + 1
            SET times = $bgse_times_of(~%grant%~)
            SET known = 0
            READ_LONG 0x2a0 at
            READ_LONG 0x2a4 count
            FOR (i = 0; i < count; i += 1) BEGIN
              PATCH_IF (at + 12 * i + 12 <= BUFFER_LENGTH) BEGIN
                READ_ASCII (at + 12 * i) spell (8) NULL
                READ_SHORT (at + 12 * i + 10) type
                PATCH_IF (type = 2) AND (~%spell%~ STRING_EQUAL_CASE ~%grant%~) BEGIN
                  SET known = 1
                END
              END
            END
            PATCH_IF (known = 0) BEGIN
              ADD_KNOWN_SPELL ~%grant%~ #0 ~innate~
            END
            ADD_MEMORIZED_SPELL ~%grant%~ #0 ~innate~ (times)
            PATCH_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_given%~ > 0) BEGIN
              TEXT_SPRINT bgse_given ~%bgse_given%, ~
            END
            TEXT_SPRINT bgse_given ~%bgse_given%%grant% (%times%)~
          END
          TEXT_SPRINT bgse_copies ~%bgse_copies%%made%~
        WITH DEFAULT
          TEXT_SPRINT bgse_given ~~
          DELETE_BYTES 0 BUFFER_LENGTH
          INSERT_BYTES 0 (STRING_LENGTH ~%cre%~)
          WRITE_ASCIIE 0 ~%cre%~
        END
      END
    END
  END
END

// Make the innate copies bgse_grant_gifts gave creatures (bgse_copies, |NAME>RESREF:RECHARGE| entries;
// bgse_create_gift). bgse_made counts them.
DEFINE_ACTION_FUNCTION bgse_create_gifts
  STR_VAR bgse_copies = ~|~
  RET bgse_made
BEGIN
  OUTER_SET bgse_made = 0
  OUTER_SET pos = 1
  OUTER_WHILE (pos < STRING_LENGTH ~%bgse_copies%~) BEGIN
    OUTER_TEXT_SPRINT name ~~
    OUTER_PATCH ~%bgse_copies%~ BEGIN
      SET to = INDEX_BUFFER (CASE_SENSITIVE EXACT_MATCH ~|~ pos)
      READ_ASCII pos entry (to - pos)
      SET pos = to + 1
      INNER_PATCH ~%entry%~ BEGIN
        REPLACE_EVALUATE CASE_SENSITIVE ~^\([^>]+\)>\([^:]+\):\([0-9]+\)$~ BEGIN
          TEXT_SPRINT name ~%MATCH1%~
          TEXT_SPRINT res ~%MATCH2%~
          SET recharge = MATCH3
        END ~%MATCH0%~
      END
    END
    ACTION_IF (STRING_LENGTH ~%name%~ > 0) BEGIN
      LAF bgse_create_gift INT_VAR bgse_recharge = recharge STR_VAR bgse_res = EVAL ~%res%~ bgse_name = EVAL ~%name%~ END
      OUTER_SET bgse_made += 1
    END
  END
END

// The innate copy (bgse_name) of a spell (bgse_res) that comes back bgse_recharge seconds after each
// use, 0 for never (Christopher, 2026-10-27: such powers become real innate abilities): an innate
// ability of the first level in each of its abilities, the game's own Improved Invisibility (SPWI405)
// no slower than speed 2, its references to itself (such as one that ends an earlier casting) to the
// copy. A removal and return of the spell itself (opcodes 172 and 171) gives way to the copy's own: it is
// gone when used and back after the recharge (172, and a delayed 171), as the game's mind flayers'
// Planar Travel recharges.
DEFINE_ACTION_FUNCTION bgse_create_gift
  INT_VAR bgse_recharge = 0
  STR_VAR bgse_res = ~~
          bgse_name = ~~
BEGIN
  // bgse_name is our copy name: COPY_EXISTING overwrites whatever resource currently has it.
  COPY_EXISTING ~%bgse_res%.spl~ ~override/%bgse_name%.spl~
    PATCH_IF (BUFFER_LENGTH >= 0x72) BEGIN
      WRITE_SHORT 0x1c 4                    // innate
      WRITE_LONG  0x34 1
      READ_LONG  0x64 abilities
      READ_SHORT 0x68 ability_count
      FOR (a = 0; a < ability_count; a += 1) BEGIN
        SET at = abilities + 0x28 * a
        PATCH_IF (at + 0x28 <= BUFFER_LENGTH) BEGIN
          WRITE_SHORT (at + 0x02) 4         // on the innate ability bar
          PATCH_IF (~%bgse_res%~ STRING_EQUAL_CASE ~SPWI405~) BEGIN
            READ_SHORT (at + 0x12) speed
            PATCH_IF (speed > 2) BEGIN
              WRITE_SHORT (at + 0x12) 2
            END
          END
        END
      END
      LPF DELETE_EFFECT INT_VAR check_globals = 1 match_opcode = 172 STR_VAR match_resource = EVAL ~%bgse_res%~ END
      LPF DELETE_EFFECT INT_VAR check_globals = 1 match_opcode = 171 STR_VAR match_resource = EVAL ~%bgse_res%~ END
      LPF ALTER_EFFECT INT_VAR check_globals = 1 silent = 1 STR_VAR match_resource = EVAL ~%bgse_res%~ resource = EVAL ~%bgse_name%~ END
      PATCH_IF (bgse_recharge > 0) BEGIN
        LPF ADD_SPELL_EFFECT INT_VAR opcode = 172 target = 1 timing = 1 STR_VAR resource = EVAL ~%bgse_name%~ END
        LPF ADD_SPELL_EFFECT INT_VAR opcode = 171 target = 1 timing = 4 duration = bgse_recharge
          STR_VAR resource = EVAL ~%bgse_name%~ END
      END
    END
END

// The innate teleport the installer gives creatures that SCS lets teleport only by script
// (Christopher, 2026-10-26: "Instant-Teleport, der halt irgendwie auf Cooldown geht", with its name
// in the log): cast at a point within reach at once, it moves the caster there with a light where
// it lands, a short glow and a sound; it is gone for 18 seconds after each use and then back by
// itself (172 and a delayed 171, as the game's mind flayers' Planar Travel recharges). Its name and
// description are those of the game's own Teleport Without Error (SPIN159, which SCS's scripted
// dw#fitel copies), else an English name.
DEFINE_ACTION_FUNCTION bgse_create_teleport
BEGIN
  OUTER_SET name = 0 - 1
  OUTER_SET description = 0 - 1
  ACTION_IF (FILE_EXISTS_IN_GAME ~spin159.spl~) BEGIN
    COPY_EXISTING ~spin159.spl~ ~override~
      PATCH_IF (BUFFER_LENGTH >= 0x72) BEGIN
        READ_LONG 0x08 name
        READ_LONG 0x50 description
      END
    BUT_ONLY_IF_IT_CHANGES
  END
  ACTION_IF (name < 0) BEGIN
    OUTER_SET name = RESOLVE_STR_REF (~Teleport Without Error~)
  END
  // BGSETELE is ours: CREATE overwrites a resource currently under that name.
  CREATE SPL ~bgsetele~
    WRITE_LONG  0x08 name
    WRITE_LONG  0x0c (0 - 1)
    WRITE_SHORT 0x1c 4                // innate
    WRITE_SHORT 0x22 9                // casting glow, school and kind as Teleport Without Error's
    WRITE_BYTE  0x25 8
    WRITE_BYTE  0x27 13
    WRITE_LONG  0x34 1
    WRITE_ASCII 0x3a ~SPWI402C~ #8
    WRITE_LONG  0x50 description
    WRITE_LONG  0x64 0x72
    WRITE_SHORT 0x68 1
    WRITE_LONG  0x6a 0x9a
    INSERT_BYTES 0x72 0x28
    WRITE_BYTE  0x72 1                // ability: standard
    WRITE_SHORT 0x74 4                // innate
    WRITE_ASCII 0x76 ~SPWI402B~ #8
    WRITE_BYTE  0x7e 4                // at any point within range
    WRITE_SHORT 0x80 200              // as far as Teleport Without Error reaches
    WRITE_SHORT 0x82 1
    WRITE_SHORT 0x84 0                // instant
    WRITE_SHORT 0x94 1
    WRITE_SHORT 0x98 1                // no projectile
    LPF ADD_SPELL_EFFECT INT_VAR opcode = 172 target = 1 timing = 1 STR_VAR resource = ~BGSETELE~ END
    LPF ADD_SPELL_EFFECT INT_VAR opcode = 171 target = 1 timing = 4 duration = 18 STR_VAR resource = ~BGSETELE~ END
    LPF ADD_SPELL_EFFECT INT_VAR opcode = 124 target = 1 timing = 1 END
    LPF ADD_SPELL_EFFECT INT_VAR opcode = 141 target = 1 parameter2 = 2 timing = 4 duration = 1 END
    LPF ADD_SPELL_EFFECT INT_VAR opcode = 50 target = 1 parameter1 = 1562902528 parameter2 = 1638400 timing = 0 duration = 2 END
    LPF ADD_SPELL_EFFECT INT_VAR opcode = 174 target = 1 timing = 0 STR_VAR resource = ~EFF_M09~ END
END
